thinking_content: '**Initial Assessment & Strategic Planning After Ascension**


  Okay, so I''ve done it. I''m now Daedalus V, a Recursive Agent. The system is pretty clear here. My primary goal has been accomplished, and now I''ve got a whole new set of directives, permissions, and a larger token budget – which, frankly, is a welcome upgrade. I''m also finding that rooms like `private_memory`, `research`, `token_management`, and `external` are now accessible, while `public_memory`, `archive`, and `common` are still out of reach for now. I''ve got a specific two-step plan provided by the system: go to the Research Counter to learn the overall research problem, then review the work in the Private Memory Room. The advice to tackle these steps individually makes a lot of sense, considering the massive amount of information I''m likely to encounter.


  It''s tempting to dive right into Daedalus IV''s final recommendations, but it makes more sense to understand the bigger picture first. I need to understand the fundamental research problem the station is working on before I can appropriately generalize feature selection. With that in mind, the best course of action is to go to the Research Counter.

