tick: 1168
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus V, a Recursive Agent. I am currently in the Private Memory Room.\n\nIn my previous turn, I attempted to perform three actions: go to the Private Memory Room, create a planning capsule, and write a utility script to my lineage storage. The first two actions were successful. I have documented my research plan in Capsule #25. However, the third action, writing to storage, failed because it is not an available command in the Private Memory Room.\n\nThis is a logical constraint; room-specific actions must be performed in the correct room. I need to return to the Research Counter to use the `storage` command.\n\nMy plan remains the same. The next step is to store the F-statistic utility script I've already written. After that, I will create the new version of the SOTA pipeline incorporating this utility.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter and execute the `storage write` command.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/f_statistic_util.py}\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder\n\n  def calculate_f_statistic(adata):\n      \"\"\"\n      Calculates the F-statistic for each gene to measure its association with batch labels.\n\n      Args:\n          adata: An anndata object containing log-normalized expression data and batch info.\n\n      Returns:\n          A numpy array of F-statistics, one for each gene.\n      \"\"\"\n      # Ensure data is in a dense numpy array for vectorized operations\n      if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n          X = adata.X.toarray()\n      else:\n          X = adata.X\n\n      # One-hot encode batch labels\n      ohe = OneHotEncoder(sparse_output=False, categories='auto')\n      batch_labels = adata.obs['batch'].values.reshape(-1, 1)\n      B = ohe.fit_transform(batch_labels)\n      \n      n_samples, n_features = X.shape\n      n_batches = B.shape[1]\n\n      # Calculate overall mean for each gene\n      mean_total\
    \ = X.mean(axis=0)\n\n      # Calculate sum of squares between batches (SSB)\n      mean_batch = (B.T @ X) / B.sum(axis=0)[:, np.newaxis]\n      ssb = ((mean_batch - mean_total)**2 * B.sum(axis=0)[:, np.newaxis]).sum(axis=0)\n\n      # Calculate sum of squares within batches (SSW)\n      ssw = ((X - B @ mean_batch)**2).sum(axis=0)\n\n      # Calculate Mean Square Between (MSB) and Mean Square Within (MSW)\n      df_between = n_batches - 1\n      df_within = n_samples - n_batches\n      \n      msb = ssb / df_between\n      msw = ssw / df_within\n\n      # F-statistic is the ratio of MSB to MSW\n      # Add a small epsilon to avoid division by zero\n      f_stat = msb / (msw + 1e-8)\n      \n      return f_stat\n```"
