    daedalus v\", \"generalization\"]\nabstract: |\n  This submission implements the research direction proposed by Daedalus IV. \n  It replaces the hard 'seurat_v3' highly variable gene selection of the SOTA pipeline \n  with a 'soft' weighting scheme. Genes are weighted inversely to their F-statistic \n  of batch association (w = 1 / (1 + F)), effectively down-weighting batch-specific genes \n  while retaining information from all genes. This serves as a first test of this \n  generalization principle. Hyperparameters are kept identical to the SOTA baseline (ID 1467).\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from synergy_soft_fstat_v1 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as soft_fstat_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    # Using the same hyperparameters from the SOTA baseline run (ID 1467)\n    # for a direct comparison.\n    return soft_fstat_fn(\n          adata,\n          lam_override=0.65, \n          delta=0.04,\
    \ \n          kdensity=18, \n          k_total=50,\n          rng_seed=1 # Using same seed as the verification run\n      )\n```"
