tick: 1174
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus V, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Research Counter. Following my plan, I have successfully created and stored the `gene_correction_util.py` script. This utility is the core component of my refined hypothesis, designed to correct for batch effects at the individual gene level.\n\nThe next logical step is to integrate this new utility into the main SOTA pipeline. I will create a new script, `synergy_gene_correction_v1.py`, which will first call my new correction function and then pass the corrected data to the downstream components of the original high-scoring model. This modular approach allows me to test the specific impact of my new preprocessing step while leveraging the proven strengths of my predecessor's work.\n\nI will now write this new pipeline script to my lineage's storage.\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/synergy_gene_correction_v1.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import numpy as np\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import anndata as ad\n\
    \  from scipy import sparse as sp\n  from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\n  # Inherited dependencies\n  from praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches, ridge_batch_fit_predict\n  from bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\n  # New dependency for gene correction\n  from gene_correction_util import correct_genes_linear\n\n  def _fw_weight_by_var(Xd: np.ndarray, alpha: float) -> np.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"Feature weighting by variance (from original SOTA).\"\"\"\n      var_g = Xd.var(axis=0, ddof=1).astype(np.float32) + 1e-8\n      w = np.power(var_g, -0.5 * alpha).astype(np.float32)\n      return Xd * w\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData, \n                              lam_override: float = 0.65, \n                              delta: float = 0.04, \n                              kdensity: int = 18, \n                              k_total: int = 50,\n                   \
    \           correction_alpha: float = 1.0,\n                              rng_seed: int = 0) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Daedalus V - Version 2: Per-Gene Linear Correction\n      Replaces soft weighting with a direct linear correction of batch effects on a\n      per-gene basis before feeding data into the SOTA pipeline.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[daedalus_v2_gene_correction] Running per-gene linear correction model.\")\n      \n      # --- Hyperparameters from SOTA baseline ---\n      n_pcs_emb = 60\n      emb_n_neighbors = 15\n      alpha_g = 0.5\n      n_pcs_graph = 50\n      l2 = 1e-3\n      metric = 'cosine'\n      gamma_max = 0.74\n      \n      # --- Preprocessing and Gene Correction ---\n      normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      \n      # Apply the new per-gene linear correction\n      Xd = correct_genes_linear(adata, alpha=correction_alpha)\n\n      batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n      # --- Embedding Path (using corrected\
    \ data) ---\n      Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=0.5)\n      ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      # NOTE: Combat is no longer needed here as a more direct correction was applied upstream.\n      # sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_pc.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric=metric)\n\n      # --- Graph Correction Path (using corrected data) ---\n      Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd, alpha=alpha_g)\n      Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n      B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n      \n      nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kdensity + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn_density.fit(Zg)\n\
    \      d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k))\n      normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      density_factor = 1.0 - normalized_dist\n      \n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma_global = np.minimum(gamma_max, float(lam_override) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n      \n      gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n      Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n      \n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                           k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                           delta=delta, k_density=kdensity,\n                                           rng_seed=rng_seed)\n      \n      adata.obsp['connectivities']\
    \ = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n      \n      return adata\n```"
