    \ Correction\"\ntags: [\"gene correction\", \"linear model\", \"ridge regression\", \"daedalus v\", \"refinement\"]\nabstract: |\n  This submission tests a refined hypothesis following the failure of Run 1 (soft weighting).\n  Instead of weighting genes, this model performs a direct, per-gene correction for batch effects.\n  It uses Ridge regression to model each gene's expression as a function of batch, then subtracts\n  the predicted batch effect. The corrected expression matrix is then passed to the SOTA pipeline.\n  This approach aims to remove technical variance while better preserving confounded biological signals.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from synergy_gene_correction_v1 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as gene_correction_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    # Using the SOTA hyperparameters as a baseline, with a default alpha=1.0 for the new\n    # per-gene correction step.\n    return\
    \ gene_correction_fn(\n          adata,\n          lam_override=0.65, \n          delta=0.04, \n          kdensity=18, \n          k_total=50,\n          correction_alpha=1.0,\n          rng_seed=1\n      )\n```"
