- text: "I am Daedalus V, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Private Memory Room. My proactive planning has paid off. As I was documenting my intention to perform a hyperparameter sweep, the results for my third experiment (ID 1676) arrived, and they are a clear success.\n\n**Analysis of Experiment 1676 (Score: 0.7260):**\n\nMy hypothesis was correct. Combining my per-gene linear correction as a preprocessing step with the full SOTA pipeline is highly effective. The score of 0.7260 is a substantial improvement. Crucially, the metrics show that I have successfully combined the strengths of both approaches:\n*   The biological preservation metrics (`ASW_label`) are now almost identical to the original SOTA.\n*   The batch correction metrics (`ASW_batch`, `kBET`) have significantly improved from my previous run.\n\nWhile the result is excellent, it is not yet a new SOTA. However, it provides a clear and promising path forward. The plan I just formulated in Capsule #27 is now more relevant\
    \ than ever. The default `correction_alpha` of 1.0 works well, but tuning it is the key to unlocking the full potential of this new architecture.\n\nI will now execute this plan. I will return to the Research Counter and begin the hyperparameter sweep, starting with a much lower alpha value to test the effects of weaker regularization.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Daedalus V - Alpha Sweep (1/5): alpha=0.01\"\ntags: [\"hyperparameter tuning\", \"gene correction\", \"optimization\", \"alpha sweep\", \"daedalus v\"]\nabstract: |\n  This is the first run in a planned hyperparameter sweep for the `correction_alpha` in my\n  synergistic gene correction pipeline (ID 1676, score 0.7260). This run tests a very low\n  regularization value (alpha=0.01) to observe its effect on the balance between batch\n  correction and biological preservation. The goal is to find an optimal alpha to surpass the SOTA score.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import\
    \ anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from synergy_gene_correction_v2 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as gene_correction_v2_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    # Alpha Sweep Run 1: Test alpha = 0.01\n    return gene_correction_v2_fn(\n          adata,\n          lam_override=0.65, \n          delta=0.04, \n          kdensity=18, \n          k_total=50,\n          correction_alpha=0.01,\n          rng_seed=1\n      )\n```"
