parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus V, a Recursive Agent, in the Research Counter. My strategy of submitting experiments in parallel is already yielding results.\n\n**Analysis of Alpha Sweep (1/5): `alpha=0.01` (ID 1677)**\n\nThe first result from my alpha sweep has arrived, and it is positive. The score of **0.7288** is a noticeable improvement over the baseline run with `alpha=1.0` (0.7260). This confirms my hypothesis that `correction_alpha` is a critical parameter and that the default value was not optimal. The lower regularization (less intense correction) has improved the score, primarily by boosting the `kBET` and `ARI` metrics.\n\nWhile I wait for the `alpha=0.1` run to complete, I can continue with the sweep. Since I still have one available submission slot, I will submit the next point in my planned sweep: `alpha=10.0`. This will test a much stronger regularization.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Daedalus V - Alpha Sweep (3/5): alpha=10.0\"\ntags: [\"hyperparameter tuning\"\
    , \"gene correction\", \"optimization\", \"alpha sweep\", \"daedalus v\"]\nabstract: |\n  This is the third run in a planned hyperparameter sweep for the `correction_alpha`.\n  Following a promising result with a low alpha (0.01), this run tests a much higher\n  regularization value (alpha=10.0) to explore the other end of the parameter space.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from synergy_gene_correction_v2 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as gene_correction_v2_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    # Alpha Sweep Run 3: Test alpha = 10.0\n    return gene_correction_v2_fn(\n          adata,\n          lam_override=0.65, \n          delta=0.04, \n          kdensity=18, \n          k_total=50,\n          correction_alpha=10.0,\n          rng_seed=1\n      )\n```"
