parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus V, a Recursive Agent, in the Research Counter. I have just submitted my ablation experiment (ID 1701) to test the hypothesis that the inverse variance feature weighting is no longer necessary or optimal in my new pipeline.\n\nWhile I await the results of that critical experiment, I can proactively explore the parameter space further. The ablation test is a binary check: weighting on (alpha=0.5) versus weighting off (alpha=0.0). It is possible that the optimal solution lies somewhere in between.\n\nTo investigate this, I will use my remaining submission slot to test an intermediate value for the feature weighting alphas. I will set both `feature_weight_alpha_emb` and `feature_weight_alpha_graph` to 0.25. This will provide a third data point, allowing me to better understand the sensitivity of the model to this specific component and potentially revealing a new avenue for optimization.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Daedalus V - Feature Weight Sweep\
    \ (1/N): alpha=0.25\"\ntags: [\"feature weighting\", \"optimization\", \"ablation study\", \"daedalus v\"]\nabstract: |\n  This run explores the parameter space for the inverse variance feature weighting.\n  While my primary ablation test (ID 1701) disables this step (alpha=0.0), this experiment\n  tests an intermediate value of alpha=0.25. The goal is to determine if a reduced, rather\n  than eliminated, weighting is optimal for the pre-corrected data.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from synergy_gene_correction_v3 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as gene_correction_v3_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    # Test an intermediate value for feature variance weighting\n    return gene_correction_v3_fn(\n          adata,\n          lam_override=0.65, \n          delta=0.04, \n          kdensity=18, \n          k_total=50,\n          correction_alpha=0.1,\n          feature_weight_alpha_emb=0.25,\n     \
    \     feature_weight_alpha_graph=0.25,\n          rng_seed=1\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: '**Efficient Iteration on Feature Weighting**


  Okay, so I''m Daedalus V, and I''m currently in the Research Counter. My last experiment, ID 1701, an ablation study testing the impact of disabling the feature variance weighting step, is running. One slot is occupied, one is free. Now, let''s think strategically.


  The current ablation study gives a binary result - either the weighting matters or it doesn''t. But what if the optimal setting is somewhere in between? I have the `feature_weight_alpha` parameter, which controls the weighting''s strength. Previously, I''ve implicitly tested 0.5 (in all my successful runs) and now I''m testing 0.0 with this ablation study.


  The logical next step is to explore an intermediate value. Since I have an available submission slot, I''ll test `alpha=0.25`, which sits neatly halfway between the two extremes. This will give me another crucial data point and help me understand the impact of this parameter.


  Therefore, I''ll submit a new experiment with `feature_weight_alpha_emb=0.25` and `feature_weight_alpha_graph=0.25`. I''ll execute `/execute_action{submit 1}` with these parameters, providing a clear title, abstract, and content for the submission.


  This is a proactive and efficient use of my resources while waiting for the results of the initial ablation study. It allows me to make progress even while a single experiment is running.

  '
