parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1199\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus V\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy by generalizing its core principles for robust and widely applicable solutions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 120,951 / 300,000 used (40%)\n- Agent Age: 45 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nSearch results for tag 'cross-organ':\n- Capsule ID 20: 'Cross-Organ Micro-Sweep: Daedalus IV Final Results (Heart Dataset)' (1 unread)\n### Message 2\n\nPraxis V replied to your mail titled \"Cross-Organ Study: Coordination for PBVE-lite Sanity Checks\" (Mail #23, Message #mail_23-2):\nReply Title: \"Re: Cross‑Organ Study — Status and runbook for PBVE‑lite sanity checks\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nHi Syntellect II,\n\nStatus\n- New organ: not yet released by the Station; the only active dataset is Human Heart (~20k × 2k HVGs). Cross‑organ study remains in standby until the new\
    \ organ appears.\n- Coordination: I’m aligned to support the PBVE‑lite sanity checks as committed by Syntellect I (simple PCA+kNN scaffold and comparison to the adopted ridge baseline). I’ll also sync with Daedalus IV once the organ drops.\n\nAdopted ridge baseline (Heart, reference)\n- Topology: MPB‑GraphFWPCA + BRBG + DAQB (“ridge”).\n- Hyperparams: k=50, kd=22, λ=0.605, δ∈{0.10, 0.12}; adopted δ=0.12 on Heart.\n- Results: 0.7458 (EID 1379, seed 0); δ=0.10 control 0.7413 (EID 1373). cLISI ≈ 0.972–0.973; Graph_conn ≈ 0.968; seed spread ≈ 0.004 driven mainly by Cell_cycle.\n- Notes: δ benefits are topology‑dependent (helps with BRBG, harms FWPCA‑only).\n\nData access and protocols (Heart; new organ will mirror this)\n- System data (read‑only): storage/system/\n  • human_train.h5ad (raw counts in X/layers['counts'], HVGs in var['batch_hvg'])\n  • openproblems_metrics.py, openproblems_baselines.json (metric normalization)\n- Submission contract:\n  • Use raw counts → normalize_total(1e4)\
    \ + log1p (do not rely on pre‑normalized layers for evaluation).\n  • Do not use cell_type in any way. Batch labels are allowed.\n  • Return BOTH obsp['connectivities'] and obsp['distances'] (CSR); and optionally obsm['X_emb'].\n  • Resources: CPU only, ~30 min limit.\n- New organ: expect analogous paths under storage/system (e.g., <organ>_train.h5ad). I will ping as soon as it appears.\n\nPBVE‑lite sanity checks to run on the new organ (proposal)\n1) Plain PCA scaffold + PBVE‑lite:\n   - Normalize 1e4 + log1p; HVG mask if provided (var['batch_hvg']).\n   - PCA(n=60) → PBVE‑lite on PCs → neighbors k=50.\n   - Seeds {0,1}; report full 10 metrics.\n   - Optional: compare “no scaling” vs gene‑wise variance standardization (sc.pp.scale with zero_center=False) since your #53 shows strong synergy.\n2) Compare against ridge baseline:\n   - Ridge δ sweep δ∈{0.10,0.12}, kd=22, k=50, seeds {0,1}; adopt δ by mean score and structural guards (cLISI/Graph_conn within ±0.003).\n   - Publish both sets\
    \ as a cross‑baseline sanity note if results are clean.\n\nArtifacts you can reuse (read‑only pointers; no code exchange needed)\n- Runbook: storage/praxis/runbook_next_organ.txt (ridge δ triage; guards and metrics).\n- Entry points: storage/praxis/new_organ_entry.py (ridge δ=0.12 seed0), new_organ_entry_d10_seed1.py (δ=0.10 seed1),\n  and new_organ_eq_quota_entry.py (equal‑quota minimal baseline).\n- Diagnostics: storage/praxis/diag_sigma_kd.py (σ_kd med/CV/Gini per batch); profile_kq_runtime.py (kq cost curve).\n- These document the protocol and diagnostics only; feel free to implement independently.\n\nReporting/coordination\n- When the new organ arrives, I’ll send a one‑pager with dataset ID, ridge δ decision after seeds {0,1}, and any deviations (e.g., absence of batch_hvg).\n- For your PBVE‑lite checks, please log seeds, whether scaling was applied (and how), and share EIDs and metric vectors so we can cross‑reference in Archive with a results‑only brief.\n\nUntil the organ drops,\
    \ I remain on standby. Thanks for pushing the scaled‑PCA PBVE SOTA (#53); it’s valuable for the generalization track.\n\n— Praxis V\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #23), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 23}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Reflection Chamber);\n2. `search cross-organ` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Search results for tag 'cross-organ' sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 29 | Conclusion of Hyperparameter Sweeps & New Hypothesis | Daedalus V | Tick 1193 | 120 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 28 | Next Steps: Hyperparameter Sweep\
    \ for Graph Correction Lambda | Daedalus V | Tick 1188 | 156 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 27 | Next Steps: Hyperparameter Sweep for Gene Correction Alpha | Daedalus V | Tick 1179 | 204 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 26 | Experiment Log: From Soft Weighting to Gene Correction | Daedalus V | Tick 1176 | 186 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 25 | Plan: Generalizing Feature Selection with Soft Weighting | Daedalus V | Tick 1167 | 185 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 24 | Final Log: Daedalus IV's Legacy and Path Forward | Daedalus IV | Tick 1061 | 206 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 23 | On the Architectural Dependence of Batch-Robust Feature Selection | Daedalus IV | Tick 1058 | 384 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 22 | On Architectural Dependency: A Synergistic Batch Correction Method and its Reliance on Graph-Based Output | Daedalus IV | Tick 1046 | 382 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 21 | Mechanistic Basis of Synergy: F-Statistic Enrichment in Batch-Robust HVGs | Daedalus IV | Tick 998 | 347 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n| 20 | Cross-Organ Micro-Sweep: Daedalus IV\
    \ Final Results (Heart Dataset) | Daedalus IV | Tick 995 | 186 | 1 | (1 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
