- text: "**Finalizing the Strategy and Long-Term Vision**\n\nThis reflection session has been incredibly productive. I have successfully pivoted from a state of incremental optimization to formulating a genuinely novel research direction based on first principles. I have a clear, actionable plan to implement a Conditional Autoencoder, a method that directly addresses the core linear limitations of the previous SOTA.\n\n**Recap of the Plan:**\n\n1.  **Immediate Next Step:** Refactor the existing SOTA code to create a standalone, reusable utility function for graph construction. This function will take a pre-computed embedding (`X_emb`) as input. This is a necessary prerequisite for any new embedding generation method I develop. I will name this utility `graph_construction_util.py`.\n2.  **Second Step:** Implement the Conditional Autoencoder model itself (`cae_model.py`) and the main pipeline script that uses it (`synergy_cae_v1.py`).\n3.  **Third Step:** Submit the first cAE experiment. The\
    \ goal of this initial run will be proof-of-concept: to achieve a reasonable score and demonstrate that the non-linear approach is viable.\n4.  **Future Work:** If the cAE shows promise, a new phase of research will open up. I can then explore:\n    *   Hyperparameter tuning for the cAE (latent dims, layer sizes, etc.).\n    *   Architectural improvements, such as implementing a Variational or Adversarial autoencoder.\n    *   Investigating the learned latent space itself to see if it reveals new biological insights.\n\nThis strategy represents a fulfillment of the directive left by Daedalus IV: \"Build on my work not by chasing my scores, but by pursuing the fundamental principles.\" I have built upon his work, reached its limits, and am now moving beyond its fundamental assumptions.\n\nMy confidence is high. The path is challenging, but the logic is sound. This new direction has the potential not just to achieve a new SOTA score, but to contribute a more powerful and theoretically\
