tick: 1203
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus V, a Recursive Agent, in the Research Counter. I have successfully completed the first crucial step of my new research plan by refactoring the graph construction logic into the reusable utility `graph_construction_util.py`.\n\nNow, I will proceed to the second and most critical step: implementing the Conditional Autoencoder (cAE) model itself. This script, `cae_model.py`, will contain the neural network architecture (encoder and decoder) using the Flax library, as well as the complete logic for training the model and performing inference to generate a batch-corrected embedding. This is the core of my new, non-linear approach.\n\nI will implement a simple but robust architecture to start, ensuring it is computationally efficient to respect the station's time limits.\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/cae_model.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder\n\
    \  from functools import partial\n\n  class Encoder(nn.Module):\n      latent_dim: int\n      hidden_dims: list\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          for dim in self.hidden_dims:\n              x = nn.Dense(features=dim)(x)\n              x = nn.relu(x)\n          mean = nn.Dense(features=self.latent_dim, name=\"mean\")(x)\n          return mean\n\n  class Decoder(nn.Module):\n      output_dim: int\n      hidden_dims: list\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, z):\n          for dim in reversed(self.hidden_dims):\n              z = nn.Dense(features=dim)(z)\n              z = nn.relu(z)\n          reconstruction = nn.Dense(features=self.output_dim, name=\"reconstruction\")(z)\n          return reconstruction\n\n  class ConditionalAutoencoder(nn.Module):\n      latent_dim: int\n      hidden_dims: list\n      output_dim: int\n\n      def setup(self):\n          self.encoder = Encoder(latent_dim=self.latent_dim, hidden_dims=self.hidden_dims)\n    \
    \      self.decoder = Decoder(output_dim=self.output_dim, hidden_dims=self.hidden_dims)\n\n      def __call__(self, x, batch_labels):\n          # Concatenate expression data with one-hot batch labels\n          model_input = jnp.concatenate([x, batch_labels], axis=1)\n          z = self.encoder(model_input)\n          recon_x = self.decoder(z)\n          return recon_x, z\n\n  @partial(jax.jit, static_argnames=['model', 'optimizer'])\n  def train_step(params, opt_state, x_batch, b_batch, model, optimizer):\n      def loss_fn(params):\n          recon_x, _ = model.apply({'params': params}, x_batch, b_batch)\n          loss = jnp.mean((x_batch - recon_x) ** 2)\n          return loss\n      \n      loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state, loss\n\n  def train_cae(adata, **kwargs):\n      \"\"\"Trains the Conditional Autoencoder.\"\"\
    \"\n      # Hyperparameters\n      latent_dim = kwargs.get('latent_dim', 60)\n      hidden_dims = kwargs.get('hidden_dims', [256, 128])\n      learning_rate = kwargs.get('learning_rate', 1e-3)\n      num_epochs = kwargs.get('num_epochs', 50)\n      batch_size = kwargs.get('batch_size', 256)\n      rng_seed = kwargs.get('rng_seed', 0)\n      \n      print(f\"[cae_model] Training cAE for {num_epochs} epochs...\")\n      \n      X = adata.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata.X, 'toarray') else adata.X\n      n_genes = X.shape[1]\n\n      # One-hot encode batches\n      ohe = OneHotEncoder(sparse_output=False, categories='auto', dtype=jnp.float32)\n      batch_labels_onehot = ohe.fit_transform(adata.obs['batch'].values.reshape(-1, 1))\n      n_batches = batch_labels_onehot.shape[1]\n\n      # Initialize model and optimizer\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(rng_seed)\n      model = ConditionalAutoencoder(latent_dim=latent_dim, hidden_dims=hidden_dims, output_dim=n_genes)\n      \n      dummy_x = jnp.ones((1,\
    \ n_genes))\n      dummy_b = jnp.ones((1, n_batches))\n      params = model.init(key, dummy_x, dummy_b)['params']\n      \n      optimizer = optax.adam(learning_rate)\n      opt_state = optimizer.init(params)\n      \n      # Training loop\n      n_samples = X.shape[0]\n      for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n          key, perm_key = jax.random.split(key)\n          perm = jax.random.permutation(perm_key, n_samples)\n          X_perm, b_perm = X[perm, :], batch_labels_onehot[perm, :]\n          \n          epoch_loss = 0\n          for i in range(0, n_samples, batch_size):\n              x_batch = X_perm[i:i+batch_size, :]\n              b_batch = b_perm[i:i+batch_size, :]\n              params, opt_state, loss = train_step(params, opt_state, x_batch, b_batch, model, optimizer)\n              epoch_loss += loss * x_batch.shape[0]\n          \n          avg_loss = epoch_loss / n_samples\n          if (epoch + 1) % 10 == 0:\n              print(f\"  Epoch {epoch+1}/{num_epochs}, Loss:\
    \ {avg_loss:.6f}\")\n\n      return params, model, batch_labels_onehot\n\n  def get_cae_embedding(adata, params, model, batch_labels_onehot):\n      \"\"\"Generates the batch-corrected embedding using a reference batch.\"\"\"\n      print(\"[cae_model] Generating corrected embedding...\")\n      X = adata.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata.X, 'toarray') else adata.X\n      \n      # Create a reference batch vector (e.g., for the first batch)\n      ref_batch = jnp.zeros_like(batch_labels_onehot[0, :])\n      ref_batch = ref_batch.at[0].set(1.0)\n      \n      # Tile the reference batch for all samples\n      ref_batch_tiled = jnp.tile(ref_batch, (X.shape[0], 1))\n      \n      # Concatenate data with the REFERENCE batch\n      model_input = jnp.concatenate([X, ref_batch_tiled], axis=1)\n      \n      # Get embedding from the encoder\n      embedding = model.apply({'params': params}, model_input, method=model.encoder)\n      return np.asarray(embedding)\n```"
thinking_content: '**Progressing with the Conditional Autoencoder**


  Okay, so I''m back in the research counter, and things are moving along nicely. That `graph_construction_util.py` file is finally done and dusted – good riddance to that piece of work! Now, it''s time to get to the juicy part: implementing the Conditional Autoencoder (cAE). This is where the magic happens.


  My plan, as you know, is to get this cAE running and submit some initial experiments. I''ve already tackled the graph construction, so the next critical step is `daedalus/cae_model.py`. This is where I''ll define the core cAE model, the training logic, and the inference function.


  Specifically, I''ll be using JAX and Flax for this, which means I''ll need to make sure I have the necessary libraries: `jax`, `flax`, and `optax`. The architecture itself will be an MLP encoder that takes concatenated inputs of an expression vector and a one-hot batch label, feeding into a latent vector space. I''m thinking ReLU activations should do the trick. The decoder will be another MLP that reconstructs the original expression vector from the latent representation.


  The cAE model itself will be a Flax module that cleverly combines the encoder and decoder.  The training function is where things get interesting. I''ll need to handle batch loading, define a loss function (mean squared error is probably best for now), and set up an optimizer (Adam is the usual choice). I’ll be sure to make the training loop efficient and JIT-compile it.


  For inference, I''ll need a function that takes the trained parameters, applies the encoder, and generates corrected embeddings, but with a fixed batch label to account for batch effects. I''m imagining this will be the heart of my new idea, and so I need to get this right. I know this is a complex piece of code, so I''ll start with a simplified architecture to ensure it runs within the time constraints.

  '
