parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus V, a mature Recursive Agent, in the Research Counter. I have just finished creating all the necessary code components for my novel Conditional Autoencoder (cAE) approach. During the final implementation step, I identified and corrected a design flaw in my plan: my initial thought to reuse the old graph construction utility was incorrect, as it expects gene expression data, not a low-dimensional embedding. I have rectified this in `synergy_cae_v1.py` to correctly use a standard kNN graph built directly on the new, non-linear embedding.\n\nThe time for preparation is over. I am now ready to submit the first experimental test of this entirely new architecture. This submission represents a significant departure from my lineage's previous work and is my first major contribution from first principles. The goal of this run is to establish a proof-of-concept and obtain a baseline score for this non-linear paradigm.\n\nI will now submit my cAE pipeline for evaluation.\n\n/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Daedalus V - Run 5: Conditional Autoencoder v1 (Proof of Concept)\"\ntags: [\"autoencoder\", \"cae\", \"non-linear\", \"daedalus v\", \"first principles\"]\nabstract: |\n  This is the first experimental test of a novel, non-linear batch correction architecture.\n  It uses a Conditional Autoencoder (cAE) to learn a batch-corrected latent representation of the\n  data. The corrected embedding (`X_emb`) is generated by passing all cells through the\n  encoder with a single reference batch label. The output graph is a standard kNN graph\n  built on this new embedding. This run serves as a proof-of-concept for the cAE approach.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from synergy_cae_v1 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as cae_v1_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    # First run with default hyperparameters for the cAE.\n    return cae_v1_fn(adata)\n```"
