tick: 1207
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1207\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus V\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy by generalizing its core principles for robust and widely applicable solutions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 142,239 / 300,000 used (47%)\n- Agent Age: 53 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Daedalus V - Run 5: Conditional Autoencoder v1 (Proof of Concept)' (ID: 1711) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.4694539673338441\n**ASW_batch:** 0.593\n**ASW_label:** 0.209\n**ARI:** 0.424\n**NMI:** 0.654\n**Graph_conn:** 0.905\n**kBET:** 0.603\n**iLISI:** 0.004\n**cLISI:** 0.991\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.311\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.593  ASW_label: 0.209  ARI: 0.424  NMI: 0.654\n  Graph_conn: 0.905  kBET: 0.603  iLISI: 0.004  cLISI: 0.991\n  PCR: 0.000\
    \  Cell_cycle: 0.311\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.800643  ASW_label: 0.532309  ARI: 0.423530  NMI: 0.654596\n  Graph_conn: 0.906990  kBET: 0.578120  iLISI: 0.004185  cLISI: 0.997278\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.274223\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1711\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed all critical bugs preventing code execution. The submission now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause Analysis\n\nThe original submission (`submission.py`) had **three critical bugs** that prevented execution:\n\n### Bug 1: JAX GPU Initialization Error\n**Error**: `FAILED_PRECONDITION: No visible GPU devices`\n**Cause**: JAX attempted to initialize CUDA/GPU backend but no GPU was available in the Python sandbox environment.\n**Location**: Occurred during `jax.random.PRNGKey()` call in `cae_model.py:81`\n\n### Bug 2: Non-Hashable Static Arguments in JIT\n**Error**: `ValueError: Non-hashable static arguments are not supported`\n**Cause**: The `train_step`\
    \ function in `storage/daedalus/cae_model.py:48` was decorated with:\n```python\n@partial(jax.jit, static_argnames=['model', 'optimizer'])\n```\nHowever, Flax modules (like `ConditionalAutoencoder`) are not hashable by default and cannot be used as static arguments in JIT-compiled functions.\n**Location**: `cae_model.py:48-58`\n\n### Bug 3: Flax Module Attribute Access Pattern\n**Error**: `AttributeError: \"ConditionalAutoencoder\" object has no attribute \"encoder\"`\n**Cause**: The `get_cae_embedding` function tried to access `model.encoder` directly:\n```python\nembedding = model.apply({'params': params}, model_input, method=model.encoder)\n```\nIn Flax, submodules defined in `setup()` cannot be accessed as direct attributes outside of `init` or `apply` contexts.\n**Location**: `cae_model.py:127`\n\n### Bug 4 (Minor): Readonly JAX Array Issue\n**Issue**: JAX arrays converted to numpy can be read-only, causing issues with downstream libraries like pynndescent/numba used by scanpy.\n\
    **Impact**: Would have caused `numba.core.errors.TypingError` in scanpy's neighbors computation.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\nCreated `submission_v8.py` with the following changes:\n\n### Fix 1: Configure JAX for CPU\n```python\nimport os\n# CRITICAL: Configure JAX to use CPU before any JAX imports\nos.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n```\nThis environment variable forces JAX to use CPU backend, bypassing GPU initialization.\n\n### Fix 2: Proper JAX/Flax Pattern for JIT\nRewrote `train_cae_fixed()` to use the correct pattern:\n- Moved `train_step` function **inside** `train_cae_fixed()` to capture model in closure\n- Removed `model` and `optimizer` from function parameters and static_argnames\n- Used simple `@jax.jit` decorator without static arguments\n- Model and optimizer are now captured as closure variables, not passed as arguments\n\n**Before (buggy)**:\n```python\n@partial(jax.jit, static_argnames=['model', 'optimizer'])\ndef train_step(params, opt_state, x_batch, b_batch, model, optimizer):\n\
    \    ...\n```\n\n**After (fixed)**:\n```python\ndef train_cae_fixed(adata, **kwargs):\n    ...\n    model = ConditionalAutoencoder(...)\n    optimizer = optax.adam(learning_rate)\n\n    @jax.jit  # model and optimizer captured in closure\n    def train_step(params, opt_state, x_batch, b_batch):\n        def loss_fn(params):\n            recon_x, _ = model.apply({'params': params}, x_batch, b_batch)\n            ...\n```\n\n### Fix 3: Correct Flax Encoder Access\nRewrote `get_cae_embedding_fixed()` to properly extract embeddings:\n- Instead of accessing `model.encoder` directly, call the full model\n- Extract the embedding (z) from the model's return tuple\n- The `ConditionalAutoencoder.__call__` returns `(recon_x, z)`, so we use `z` (index 1)\n\n**Before (buggy)**:\n```python\nembedding = model.apply({'params': params}, model_input, method=model.encoder)\n```\n\n**After (fixed)**:\n```python\n_, embedding = model.apply({'params': params}, X, ref_batch_tiled)\n# Second element is the\
    \ embedding (z)\n```\n\n### Fix 4: Ensure Writable Arrays\n```python\nreturn np.array(embedding, copy=True)\n```\nExplicitly creates a writable numpy copy to avoid readonly array issues with numba.\n\n## Implementation Strategy\n\nSince the bugs were in the lineage code (`storage/daedalus/cae_model.py`), I:\n1. Copied **only the buggy functions** (`train_cae` and `get_cae_embedding`) into the submission\n2. Fixed the bugs in the copied versions (`train_cae_fixed`, `get_cae_embedding_fixed`)\n3. Kept all other working imports from the lineage code unchanged\n4. Updated `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` to call the fixed versions\n\nThis minimal-change approach ensures maximum compatibility with the rest of the agent's code while fixing only what was broken.\n\n## Verification\n\nThe monitor script confirmed success:\n- Training completed successfully (50 epochs with decreasing loss)\n- Embedding generation succeeded\n- Graph construction completed\n- Code ran for **300+ seconds without crashing**\
    \ (timeout threshold)\n- Exit code: 1 (running/success)\n\n## Technical Notes\n\n**JAX/Flax Best Practices Applied:**\n1. **Environment configuration before imports**: JAX platform must be set before any JAX modules are imported\n2. **Closure-based JIT**: Modern JAX/Flax pattern uses closures to capture model/optimizer rather than passing as static args\n3. **Proper module access**: Flax submodules must be accessed through `apply()` method, not as direct attributes\n4. **Array writability**: Always create writable copies when interfacing JAX with other libraries\n\nThese fixes align with official JAX and Flax documentation patterns for training neural networks.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v8):**\n```python\nimport os\n# CRITICAL: Configure JAX to use CPU before any JAX imports\nos.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n\nimport sys\n\
    import anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder\nfrom functools import partial\n\nsys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\n# Import what we need from lineage code (things that work correctly)\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace\nfrom cae_model import ConditionalAutoencoder\nfrom graph_construction_util import build_corrected_graph\n\ndef train_cae_fixed(adata, **kwargs):\n    \"\"\"Trains the Conditional Autoencoder with fixed train_step.\n\n    The key fix: Don't pass the model to the JIT-compiled function.\n    Instead, capture it in the closure.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Hyperparameters\n    latent_dim = kwargs.get('latent_dim', 60)\n    hidden_dims = kwargs.get('hidden_dims', [256, 128])\n    learning_rate = kwargs.get('learning_rate', 1e-3)\n    num_epochs = kwargs.get('num_epochs', 50)\n    batch_size = kwargs.get('batch_size', 256)\n    rng_seed = kwargs.get('rng_seed',\
    \ 0)\n\n    print(f\"[cae_model] Training cAE for {num_epochs} epochs...\")\n\n    X = adata.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata.X, 'toarray') else adata.X\n    n_genes = X.shape[1]\n\n    # One-hot encode batches\n    ohe = OneHotEncoder(sparse_output=False, categories='auto', dtype=jnp.float32)\n    batch_labels_onehot = ohe.fit_transform(adata.obs['batch'].values.reshape(-1, 1))\n    n_batches = batch_labels_onehot.shape[1]\n\n    # Initialize model and optimizer\n    key = jax.random.PRNGKey(rng_seed)\n    model = ConditionalAutoencoder(latent_dim=latent_dim, hidden_dims=hidden_dims, output_dim=n_genes)\n\n    dummy_x = jnp.ones((1, n_genes))\n    dummy_b = jnp.ones((1, n_batches))\n    params = model.init(key, dummy_x, dummy_b)['params']\n\n    optimizer = optax.adam(learning_rate)\n    opt_state = optimizer.init(params)\n\n    # Define train_step inside this function to capture model in closure\n    # This is the standard JAX/Flax pattern\n    @jax.jit\n    def train_step(params, opt_state,\
    \ x_batch, b_batch):\n        def loss_fn(params):\n            recon_x, _ = model.apply({'params': params}, x_batch, b_batch)\n            loss = jnp.mean((x_batch - recon_x) ** 2)\n            return loss\n\n        loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n        updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state)\n        params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n        return params, opt_state, loss\n\n    # Training loop\n    n_samples = X.shape[0]\n    for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n        key, perm_key = jax.random.split(key)\n        perm = jax.random.permutation(perm_key, n_samples)\n        X_perm, b_perm = X[perm, :], batch_labels_onehot[perm, :]\n\n        epoch_loss = 0\n        for i in range(0, n_samples, batch_size):\n            x_batch = X_perm[i:i+batch_size, :]\n            b_batch = b_perm[i:i+batch_size, :]\n            # Use the train_step that captures model in closure\n            params, opt_state, loss = train_step(params, opt_state,\
    \ x_batch, b_batch)\n            epoch_loss += loss * x_batch.shape[0]\n\n        avg_loss = epoch_loss / n_samples\n        if (epoch + 1) % 10 == 0:\n            print(f\"  Epoch {epoch+1}/{num_epochs}, Loss: {avg_loss:.6f}\")\n\n    return params, model, batch_labels_onehot\n\ndef get_cae_embedding_fixed(adata, params, model, batch_labels_onehot):\n    \"\"\"Generates the batch-corrected embedding using a reference batch.\n\n    Fixed version: Access encoder through a custom method, not as model.encoder\n    Also ensures output is a writable numpy array (not readonly JAX array)\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"[cae_model] Generating corrected embedding...\")\n    X = adata.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata.X, 'toarray') else adata.X\n\n    # Create a reference batch vector (e.g., for the first batch)\n    ref_batch = jnp.zeros_like(batch_labels_onehot[0, :])\n    ref_batch = ref_batch.at[0].set(1.0)\n\n    # Tile the reference batch for all samples\n    ref_batch_tiled = jnp.tile(ref_batch, (X.shape[0],\
    \ 1))\n\n    # Get embedding from the encoder by running the full model and extracting z\n    _, embedding = model.apply({'params': params}, X, ref_batch_tiled)\n\n    # Convert to numpy array and make a writable copy to avoid readonly array issues\n    return np.array(embedding, copy=True)\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Daedalus V - Version 4: Conditional Autoencoder for Batch Correction\n\n    This pipeline replaces the entire linear correction and PCA embedding generation\n    with a non-linear Conditional Autoencoder (cAE). The cAE is trained to produce\n    a batch-aware embedding, which is then inferred using a reference batch to create\n    a corrected embedding (`X_emb`). This embedding is then used for downstream\n    kNN graph construction and the original SOTA's corrected graph construction.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"[daedalus_v4_cae] Running Conditional Autoencoder pipeline.\")\n\n    # --- cAE Hyperparameters ---\n    cae_params\
    \ = {\n        'latent_dim': 60,\n        'hidden_dims': [256, 128],\n        'learning_rate': 1e-3,\n        'num_epochs': 50,\n        'batch_size': 256,\n        'rng_seed': 1\n    }\n\n    # --- Graph Construction Hyperparameters (from previous optimum) ---\n    graph_params = {\n        'lam_override': 0.65,\n        'delta': 0.04,\n        'kdensity': 18,\n        'k_total': 50,\n        'feature_weight_alpha_graph': 0.5, # Keep the original weighting for now\n        'rng_seed': 1\n    }\n\n    # 1. Preprocessing\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n\n    # 2. Train cAE and get corrected embedding - USE FIXED VERSIONS\n    trained_params, model, onehot_batches = train_cae_fixed(adata, **cae_params)\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = get_cae_embedding_fixed(adata, trained_params, model, onehot_batches)\n\n    # 3. Build standard kNN graph on the new embedding for evaluation metrics\n    import scanpy as sc\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric='cosine')\n\
    \n    # 4. Build the more complex, corrected graph for final output\n    # NOTE: We pass the *original* normalized data `adata.X` to the graph builder,\n    # as it performs its own PCA and correction. This is a known architectural quirk.\n    # The cAE's X_emb is used for kNN and other metrics, but the graph part of the SOTA\n    # pipeline starts from scratch. We will follow this pattern.\n\n    # It is more principled to build the graph from the corrected embedding. Let's try that first.\n    # PCA on the embedding to get the input for the graph correction path.\n    from praxis_core import pca_array\n    Xd_graph = pca_array(adata.obsm['X_emb'], n_comps=50, random_state=1)\n\n    # Re-purpose the graph builder to now take this PCA'd embedding as `Xd`\n    # We will need to slightly modify the graph builder in the next version if this is not compatible.\n    # For now, let's assume it is.\n    # NO, wait. The graph builder expects gene expression. This is a design flaw in my plan.\n\
    \n    # Corrected Plan: The graph construction part of the SOTA pipeline also needs to be replaced.\n    # It relies on a linear batch correction in PCA space. A non-linear approach would be to\n    # build the graph DIRECTLY on the corrected X_emb. Let's do that.\n\n    # The `build_corrected_graph` is therefore not needed for this pure non-linear approach.\n    # I will simply return the standard kNN graph built on the cAE embedding.\n\n    print(\"[daedalus_v4_cae] Using standard kNN graph on cAE embedding.\")\n\n    # The submission format requires 'connectivities' and 'distances'.\n    # sc.pp.neighbors creates these but they need to be accessed correctly.\n    # scanpy stores them in obsp dict, we just need to make sure they exist with the right keys\n    if 'connectivities' not in adata.obsp:\n        # Copy from the keys that scanpy actually uses\n        if 'distances' in adata.obsp and 'connectivities' in adata.obsp:\n            # Already there, do nothing\n            pass\n\
    \        else:\n            # Try to find the actual keys scanpy uses\n            print(f\"[DEBUG] Available obsp keys: {list(adata.obsp.keys())}\")\n            # scanpy might use different keys, let's just rely on what scanpy created\n            pass\n\n    # Actually, scanpy pp.neighbors should already create the right keys\n    # The evaluation system will look for 'connectivities' and 'distances' which should already be there\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[daedalus_v4_cae] Running Conditional Autoencoder pipeline.\n[cae_model] Training cAE for 50 epochs...\n  Epoch 10/50, Loss: 0.604306\n  Epoch 20/50, Loss: 0.587697\n  Epoch 30/50, Loss: 0.580082\n  Epoch 40/50, Loss: 0.575612\n  Epoch 50/50, Loss: 0.572321\n\
    [cae_model] Generating corrected embedding...\n[daedalus_v4_cae] Using standard kNN graph on cAE embedding.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/fab724ed-b76d-4bf2-9256-0d8803620b0e/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: fab724ed-b76d-4bf2-9256-0d8803620b0e\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI\
