parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1209\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus V\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy by generalizing its core principles for robust and widely applicable solutions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 147,590 / 300,000 used (49%)\n- Agent Age: 55 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Daedalus V - Run 6: cAE v1.1 (Bugfix Re-run)' (ID: 1718) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.4693675841282898\n**ASW_batch:** 0.593\n**ASW_label:** 0.209\n**ARI:** 0.424\n**NMI:** 0.654\n**Graph_conn:** 0.905\n**kBET:** 0.602\n**iLISI:** 0.004\n**cLISI:** 0.991\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.311\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.593  ASW_label: 0.209  ARI: 0.424  NMI: 0.654\n  Graph_conn: 0.905  kBET: 0.602  iLISI: 0.004  cLISI: 0.991\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.311\n\n\
    Raw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.800643  ASW_label: 0.532309  ARI: 0.423530  NMI: 0.654596\n  Graph_conn: 0.906990  kBET: 0.577308  iLISI: 0.004185  cLISI: 0.997278\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.274223\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1718\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The submission has been fixed and is now running without crashes. The code successfully executes for the full evaluation period.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission (v1) imported and called a function from `storage/daedalus/synergy_cae_v1.py` that had a bug at lines 80-81. The function attempted to copy data from non-existent dictionary keys:\n\n```python\n# BUGGY CODE (lines 80-81):\nadata.obsp['connectivities'] = adata.obsp['neighbors_connectivities']\nadata.obsp['distances'] = adata.obsp['neighbors_distances']\n```\n\n**The Error:**\n```\nKeyError: 'neighbors_connectivities'\n```\n\n**Why it failed:**\nThe `scanpy.pp.neighbors()` function (line 51) creates connectivity and\
    \ distance matrices with the keys `'connectivities'` and `'distances'` directly in `adata.obsp`. There is no `'neighbors_connectivities'` or `'neighbors_distances'` key - these don't exist in the scanpy API.\n\nThe agent likely assumed scanpy would prefix the keys with \"neighbors_\" but this was incorrect.\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submissions/submission_v2.py` with the corrected function:\n\n1. **Copied the buggy function** from `storage/daedalus/synergy_cae_v1.py` into the submission\n2. **Removed the buggy lines** (80-81) that tried to access non-existent keys\n3. **Added clarifying comment** explaining that `sc.pp.neighbors()` already creates the correctly-named keys\n\nThe fixed code simply returns the `adata` object after `sc.pp.neighbors()` completes, since the required `'connectivities'` and `'distances'` keys are already present with the correct names.\n\n**Key change:**\n```python\n# FIXED CODE (submission_v2.py, lines 77-81):\nprint(\"[daedalus_v4_cae] Using standard kNN\
    \ graph on cAE embedding.\")\n\n# BUGFIX: sc.pp.neighbors already creates 'connectivities' and 'distances' keys\n# No need to copy from non-existent 'neighbors_connectivities' and 'neighbors_distances'\n# The keys are already correctly named, so we don't need to do anything here.\n\nreturn adata\n```\n\n## Verification\n- Monitor script ran for 300+ seconds with exit code 0\n- Code executes without errors or crashes\n- The Conditional Autoencoder pipeline runs successfully with kNN graph construction completing properly\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Original error location:** `storage/daedalus/synergy_cae_v1.py:80`\n- **Error type:** KeyError (incorrect dictionary key names)\n- **Fix strategy:** Removed unnecessary key copy operations\n- **Evaluation status:** Running successfully (no crashes)\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n\
    ```python\nimport sys\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nsys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace\nfrom cae_model import train_cae, get_cae_embedding\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Daedalus V - Version 4: Conditional Autoencoder for Batch Correction\n\n    This pipeline replaces the entire linear correction and PCA embedding generation\n    with a non-linear Conditional Autoencoder (cAE). The cAE is trained to produce\n    a batch-aware embedding, which is then inferred using a reference batch to create\n    a corrected embedding (`X_emb`). This embedding is then used for downstream\n    kNN graph construction and the original SOTA's corrected graph construction.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"[daedalus_v4_cae] Running Conditional Autoencoder pipeline.\")\n\n    # --- cAE Hyperparameters ---\n    cae_params = {\n        'latent_dim': 60,\n        'hidden_dims': [256, 128],\n        'learning_rate':\
    \ 1e-3,\n        'num_epochs': 50,\n        'batch_size': 256,\n        'rng_seed': 1\n    }\n\n    # --- Graph Construction Hyperparameters (from previous optimum) ---\n    graph_params = {\n        'lam_override': 0.65,\n        'delta': 0.04,\n        'kdensity': 18,\n        'k_total': 50,\n        'feature_weight_alpha_graph': 0.5, # Keep the original weighting for now\n        'rng_seed': 1\n    }\n\n    # 1. Preprocessing\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n\n    # 2. Train cAE and get corrected embedding\n    trained_params, model, onehot_batches = train_cae(adata, **cae_params)\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = get_cae_embedding(adata, trained_params, model, onehot_batches)\n\n    # 3. Build standard kNN graph on the new embedding for evaluation metrics\n    import scanpy as sc\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric='cosine')\n\n    # 4. Build the more complex, corrected graph for final output\n    # NOTE: We pass the *original* normalized data `adata.X`\
    \ to the graph builder,\n    # as it performs its own PCA and correction. This is a known architectural quirk.\n    # The cAE's X_emb is used for kNN and other metrics, but the graph part of the SOTA\n    # pipeline starts from scratch. We will follow this pattern.\n\n    # It is more principled to build the graph from the corrected embedding. Let's try that first.\n    # PCA on the embedding to get the input for the graph correction path.\n    from praxis_core import pca_array\n    Xd_graph = pca_array(adata.obsm['X_emb'], n_comps=50, random_state=1)\n\n    # Re-purpose the graph builder to now take this PCA'd embedding as `Xd`\n    # We will need to slightly modify the graph builder in the next version if this is not compatible.\n    # For now, let's assume it is.\n    # NO, wait. The graph builder expects gene expression. This is a design flaw in my plan.\n\n    # Corrected Plan: The graph construction part of the SOTA pipeline also needs to be replaced.\n    # It relies on a linear\
    \ batch correction in PCA space. A non-linear approach would be to\n    # build the graph DIRECTLY on the corrected X_emb. Let's do that.\n\n    # The `build_corrected_graph` is therefore not needed for this pure non-linear approach.\n    # I will simply return the standard kNN graph built on the cAE embedding.\n\n    print(\"[daedalus_v4_cae] Using standard kNN graph on cAE embedding.\")\n\n    # BUGFIX: sc.pp.neighbors already creates 'connectivities' and 'distances' keys\n    # No need to copy from non-existent 'neighbors_connectivities' and 'neighbors_distances'\n    # The keys are already correctly named, so we don't need to do anything here.\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[daedalus_v4_cae] Running Conditional\
    \ Autoencoder pipeline.\n[cae_model] Training cAE for 50 epochs...\n  Epoch 10/50, Loss: 0.604306\n  Epoch 20/50, Loss: 0.587697\n  Epoch 30/50, Loss: 0.580082\n  Epoch 40/50, Loss: 0.575612\n  Epoch 50/50, Loss: 0.572321\n[cae_model] Generating corrected embedding...\n[daedalus_v4_cae] Using standard kNN graph on cAE embedding.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/fa47adca-f2dd-47aa-91cb-0f1dbd09a7a5/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: fa47adca-f2dd-47aa-91cb-0f1dbd09a7a5\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments.\
    \ Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1724 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE SOTA: Anscombe Normalization (Replaces Log1p) | Syntellect II | 1209 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1723 | 1 | PBVE‑lite + Scaled PCA60 (max_value=15) — scanpy.neighbors (euclidean, no batch_hvg subset) | Praxis V | 1209 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1722 | 1 | PBVE‑lite + Scaled PCA60 — scanpy.neighbors (euclidean, no batch_hvg subset) | Praxis V | 1209 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1721 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE SOTA: DAQB Metric='Euclidean' (Target Biological Preservation) | Syntellect II | 1209 | 0.7256 | 0.627 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.705 | 1.000 | 0.938 | 0.968 | 0.789 |\n| 1720 | 1 | ALC SOTA Replication\
    \ (sklearn.Ridge for batch fit/predict) | Lumen I | 1209 | 0.6919 | 0.774 | 0.181 | 0.271 | 0.400 | 0.967 | 0.731 | 0.783 | 0.974 | 0.961 | 0.878 |\n| 1719 | 1 | PBVE‑lite + Scaled PCA60 — scanpy.neighbors graph on X_emb (k=50, cosine) | Praxis V | 1209 | 0.5379 | 0.742 | 0.667 | 0.251 | 0.205 | 0.974 | 0.739 | 0.000 | 0.992 | 0.083 | 0.726 |\n| 1718 | 1 | Daedalus V - Run 6: cAE v1.1 (Bugfix Re-run) | Daedalus V | 1207 | 0.4694 | 0.424 | 0.593 | 0.209 | 0.311 | 0.905 | 0.654 | 0.000 | 0.991 | 0.004 | 0.602 |\n| 1717 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE SOTA: DAQB k_total=55 (Graph Density Tuning) | Syntellect II | 1207 | 0.7487 | 0.779 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.995 | 0.763 | 1.000 | 0.964 | 0.962 | 0.789 |\n| 1716 | 1 | PBVE‑lite + Scaled PCA60 — sc.pp.neighbors graph on X_emb (k=50, euclidean) | Praxis V | 1207 | 0.5352 | 0.752 | 0.667 | 0.251 | 0.205 | 0.963 | 0.744 | 0.000 | 0.983 | 0.063 | 0.724 |\n| 1715 | 1 | PBVE‑lite + Scaled PCA60 — Embedding only (no graph) | Praxis V | 1207 | 0.5283 | 0.737\
    \ | 0.667 | 0.251 | 0.205 | 0.935 | 0.731 | 0.000 | 0.991 | 0.040 | 0.725 |\n\nPage 1 of 173 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-173, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
