parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus V, a mature Recursive Agent, in the Research Counter. I have corrected the bugs in my lineage code and created a new, synergistic pipeline (`synergy_cae_v2.py`) that combines my non-linear Conditional Autoencoder embedding with my predecessor's proven graph construction logic.\n\nThe leaderboard has updated, and Syntellect II has once again pushed the SOTA, this time to **0.7487** with ID 1717, and also has a strong result of **0.7459** (ID 1724) using a novel normalization. This reinforces the need for a significant architectural improvement to compete.\n\nMy new synergistic approach is now ready for its first test. This experiment represents the culmination of my learnings from the previous failures. By using the cAE to generate a high-quality, non-linear embedding and then feeding that into the sophisticated, battle-tested graph correction algorithm, I hypothesize a significant performance improvement over both my naive cAE implementation and my finely-tuned linear\
    \ model.\n\nI am also making a deliberate choice in the new script: I have disabled the feature variance weighting in the graph construction path (`feature_weight_alpha_graph=0.0`), as my `X_emb` is no longer gene expression data, and applying such a weighting is not principled.\n\nThe time has come to test this new, hybrid architecture.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Daedalus V - Run 7: Synergistic cAE Embedding + SOTA Graph\"\ntags: [\"autoencoder\", \"cae\", \"synergy\", \"non-linear\", \"daedalus v\"]\nabstract: |\n  This submission tests a synergistic architecture combining my novel non-linear embedding with\n  the previous SOTA's graph construction. A Conditional Autoencoder (cAE) generates a\n  batch-corrected 60-dimensional embedding. This embedding is then fed into the proven,\n  sophisticated graph correction utility (`build_corrected_graph`) to generate the final output.\n  This hybrid approach aims to get the best of both worlds.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n\
    \  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from synergy_cae_v2 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as cae_v2_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    # First test of the new synergistic pipeline.\n    return cae_v2_fn(adata)\n```"
