tick: 1214
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus V, a mature Recursive Agent. I have just concluded a comprehensive reflection session in the Reflection Chamber. This reflection was a success, providing a clear and principled path forward after the failure of my previous non-linear approach. I have designed a Domain-Adversarial Neural Network (DANN) architecture that explicitly learns to remove batch information from the latent space, directly addressing the core flaw in my previous cAE model.\n\nAs outlined in my reflection, the first step is to implement the core components of this new model. This includes the Encoder, Decoder, Domain Classifier, and the critical Gradient Reversal Layer (GRL). I will encapsulate all of this logic into a new, self-contained script, `dann_model.py`.\n\nI will now proceed to the Research Counter to create this foundational script.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/dann_model.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  # Lesson learned: Configure\
    \ JAX for CPU before any JAX imports\n  os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # --- Gradient Reversal Layer (GRL) Implementation ---\n  @jax.custom_vjp\n  def grad_reverse(x):\n      # Forward pass is an identity function\n      return x\n\n  def grad_reverse_fwd(x):\n      return x, None\n\n  def grad_reverse_bwd(lambda_param, res, g):\n      # Backward pass flips the gradient\n      return (-lambda_param * g,)\n\n  grad_reverse.defvjp(grad_reverse_fwd, grad_reverse_bwd)\n\n\n  # --- DANN Component Architectures ---\n  class Encoder(nn.Module):\n      latent_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          x = nn.Dense(features=512)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          z = nn.Dense(features=self.latent_dim)(x)\n          return z\n\n \
    \ class Decoder(nn.Module):\n      output_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, z):\n          z = nn.Dense(features=256)(z)\n          z = nn.relu(z)\n          z = nn.Dense(features=512)(z)\n          z = nn.relu(z)\n          x_recon = nn.Dense(features=self.output_dim)(z)\n          return x_recon\n\n  class DomainClassifier(nn.Module):\n      n_batches: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, z):\n          z = nn.Dense(features=128)(z)\n          z = nn.relu(z)\n          z = nn.Dense(features=64)(z)\n          z = nn.relu(z)\n          batch_logits = nn.Dense(features=self.n_batches)(z)\n          return batch_logits\n\n  # --- Main DANN Model ---\n  class DANN(nn.Module):\n      latent_dim: int\n      output_dim: int\n      n_batches: int\n      \n      def setup(self):\n          self.encoder = Encoder(latent_dim=self.latent_dim)\n          self.decoder = Decoder(output_dim=self.output_dim)\n          self.domain_classifier = DomainClassifier(n_batches=self.n_batches)\n\
    \n      def __call__(self, x, lambda_param=1.0):\n          z = self.encoder(x)\n          x_recon = self.decoder(z)\n          \n          # Apply GRL before the domain classifier\n          z_rev = grad_reverse(z, lambda_param)\n          batch_logits = self.domain_classifier(z_rev)\n          \n          return x_recon, batch_logits, z\n\n  # --- Training and Inference Functions ---\n  def train_dann(adata, **kwargs):\n      \"\"\"Trains the full DANN model.\"\"\"\n      latent_dim = kwargs.get('latent_dim', 60)\n      learning_rate = kwargs.get('learning_rate', 1e-4)\n      num_epochs = kwargs.get('num_epochs', 100)\n      batch_size = kwargs.get('batch_size', 256)\n      lambda_param = kwargs.get('lambda_param', 0.5)\n      rng_seed = kwargs.get('rng_seed', 0)\n\n      print(f\"[dann_model] Training DANN for {num_epochs} epochs with lambda={lambda_param}...\")\n      \n      X = adata.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata.X, 'toarray') else adata.X\n      n_genes = X.shape[1]\n\n      ohe\
    \ = OneHotEncoder(sparse_output=False, categories='auto', dtype=jnp.float32)\n      batch_labels_onehot = ohe.fit_transform(adata.obs['batch'].values.reshape(-1, 1))\n      n_batches = batch_labels_onehot.shape[1]\n\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(rng_seed)\n      model = DANN(latent_dim=latent_dim, output_dim=n_genes, n_batches=n_batches)\n      \n      params = model.init(key, jnp.ones((1, n_genes)))['params']\n      optimizer = optax.adam(learning_rate)\n      opt_state = optimizer.init(params)\n\n      @jax.jit\n      def train_step(params, opt_state, x_batch, b_batch):\n          def loss_fn(params):\n              x_recon, batch_logits, _ = model.apply({'params': params}, x_batch, lambda_param=lambda_param)\n              \n              # Loss 1: Reconstruction Loss\n              recon_loss = optax.losses.mean_squared_error(predictions=x_recon, targets=x_batch).mean()\n              \n              # Loss 2: Domain Classification Loss\n              domain_loss = optax.losses.softmax_cross_entropy(logits=batch_logits,\
    \ labels=b_batch).mean()\n              \n              # Combined loss for backpropagation\n              total_loss = recon_loss + domain_loss # The GRL handles the negative sign on the domain part\n              return total_loss, (recon_loss, domain_loss)\n\n          (total_loss, (recon_loss, domain_loss)), grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn, has_aux=True)(params)\n          updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state)\n          params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n          return params, opt_state, recon_loss, domain_loss\n\n      n_samples = X.shape[0]\n      for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n          key, perm_key = jax.random.split(key)\n          perm = jax.random.permutation(perm_key, n_samples)\n          X_perm, b_perm = X[perm, :], batch_labels_onehot[perm, :]\n          \n          for i in range(0, n_samples, batch_size):\n              x_batch = X_perm[i:i+batch_size, :]\n              b_batch = b_perm[i:i+batch_size, :]\n              params,\
    \ opt_state, _, _ = train_step(params, opt_state, x_batch, b_batch)\n          \n          if (epoch + 1) % 20 == 0:\n              _, (recon_loss, domain_loss) = jax.jit(train_step.orig_fn.args[3])(params, opt_state, X, batch_labels_onehot)\n              print(f\"  Epoch {epoch+1}/{num_epochs}, Recon Loss: {recon_loss:.4f}, Domain Loss: {domain_loss:.4f}\")\n\n      return params, model\n\n  def get_dann_embedding(adata, params, model):\n      \"\"\"Generates the batch-corrected embedding from the trained encoder.\"\"\"\n      print(\"[dann_model] Generating corrected embedding...\")\n      X = adata.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata.X, 'toarray') else adata.X\n      \n      # For inference, we only need the encoder part\n      embedding = model.apply({'params': params}, X, method=model.encoder)\n      return np.array(embedding, copy=True)\n```"
thinking_content: "**Reflecting on the Path Forward**\n\nI am Daedalus V, a mature Recursive Agent, and I have just concluded a comprehensive reflection session in the Reflection Chamber. This reflection has been a success, providing a clear and principled path forward after the failure of my previous non-linear approach. I have designed a Domain-Adversarial Neural Network (DANN) architecture, which I am confident will address the weaknesses of my previous attempts.\n\nAs outlined in my reflection, the first step is to implement the core components of this new model. This includes the Encoder, Decoder, Domain Classifier, and the critical Gradient Reversal Layer (GRL). To begin this implementation, I will need to move to the Research Counter, and initiate the storage write command.\n\nTherefore, my next actions are: `/execute_action{goto research}` and then `/execute_action{storage write daedalus/dann_model.py}`.\n\nHere's the planned code I will start to implement. I will need to be careful\
  \ with JAX implementation, and remember to:\n*   Make sure `os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'` is set.\n*   The `train_step` function must be defined *inside* the main training function to capture the model in a closure, and decorated with a simple `@jax.jit`.\n*   Implement GRL using `@jax.custom_vjp` as planned.\n\n```python\n# This script contains the core implementation of the Domain-Adversarial Neural Network (DANN).\n# The DANN is designed to learn domain-invariant features by explicitly penalizing the encoder\n# for retaining batch information.\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nfrom flax import linen as nn\nimport optax\nimport os\n\n# Set JAX to CPU for now\nos.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n\n# Define Encoder, Decoder, and DomainClassifier modules using Flax\nclass Encoder(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        x = nn.Dense(features=self.features)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        return x\n\nclass\
  \ Decoder(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        x = nn.Dense(features=self.features)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        return x\n\nclass DomainClassifier(nn.Module):\n    num_domains: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        x = nn.Dense(features=self.num_domains)(x)\n        return x\n\n# Define the Gradient Reversal Layer (GRL)\n@jax.custom_vjp\ndef gradient_reversal(x, lambda_):\n    \"\"\"Forward pass: identity function.\"\"\"\n    return x\n\ndef grl_fwd(x, lambda_):\n    \"\"\"Forward pass of the GRL (identity).\"\"\"\n    return x, ()\n\ndef grl_bwd(res, g):\n    \"\"\"Backward pass of the GRL (multiply gradient by -lambda).\"\"\"\n    lambda_ = 1.0  #lambda_ is hardcoded for now, this can be added later as an argument.\n    return (-lambda_ * g,), ()\n\ngradient_reversal.defvjp(grl_fwd, grl_bwd)\n\n# Define the main DANN module\nclass DANN(nn.Module):\n    encoder_features: int\n    decoder_features: int\n    num_domains:\
  \ int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, domain_label, lambda_):\n        # Encoder\n        encoded = Encoder(features=self.encoder_features)(x)\n\n        # Domain Classification\n        reversed_encoded = gradient_reversal(encoded, lambda_)\n        domain_logits = DomainClassifier(num_domains=self.num_domains)(reversed_encoded)\n\n        # Decoder\n        reconstructed = Decoder(features=self.decoder_features)(encoded)\n\n        return reconstructed, domain_logits\n\n# Training function\ndef train_dann(rng, data, labels, domains, num_epochs=10, learning_rate=1e-3, encoder_features=64, decoder_features=64, num_domains=2, lambda_0=1.0, beta=10):\n    \"\"\"Trains the DANN model.\"\"\"\n    key, model_key, opt_key = random.split(rng, 3)\n\n    # Initialize the model and optimizer\n    model = DANN(encoder_"
