tick: 1215
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus V, a mature Recursive Agent, in the Research Counter. I have successfully created the core implementation of my new Domain-Adversarial Neural Network (DANN) and stored it as `dann_model.py`. This script contains the complete architecture and training logic for my new approach.\n\nThe leaderboard has updated again, and Syntellect II has achieved a new SOTA of **0.7489** (ID 1725). This further solidifies my conviction that a fundamental architectural shift, like the DANN I've just designed, is necessary to make a significant leap in performance.\n\nThe next and final step before I can test this new model is to create the main pipeline script, `synergy_dann_v1.py`. This script will integrate my new DANN model with my proven, refactored `graph_construction_util.py`. It will train the DANN to produce a batch-corrected embedding and then pass that embedding to the powerful graph construction logic. This is the synergistic approach my reflection concluded was the most promising.\n\
    \nI will now create this final script.\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/synergy_dann_v1.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\n  from praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace\n  from dann_model import train_dann, get_dann_embedding\n  from graph_construction_util import build_corrected_graph\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Daedalus V - Version 6: Domain-Adversarial Neural Network (DANN)\n      \n      This pipeline uses a DANN to learn a batch-invariant embedding. The DANN\n      consists of an encoder, a decoder (for reconstruction), and a domain\n      classifier (adversary). The encoder is trained to fool the classifier,\n      forcing the embedding to be batch-agnostic. This embedding is then used\n      by the proven `build_corrected_graph` utility.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[daedalus_v6_dann] Running DANN synergistic pipeline.\")\n      \n  \
    \    # --- DANN Hyperparameters (for first proof-of-concept run) ---\n      dann_params = {\n          'latent_dim': 60,\n          'learning_rate': 1e-4,\n          'num_epochs': 100,\n          'batch_size': 256,\n          'lambda_param': 0.5, # Adversarial weight\n          'rng_seed': 1\n      }\n      \n      # --- Graph Construction Hyperparameters (from previous optimum) ---\n      graph_params = {\n          'lam_override': 0.65,\n          'delta': 0.04,\n          'kdensity': 18,\n          'k_total': 50,\n          'feature_weight_alpha_graph': 0.0, # No variance weighting on the embedding\n          'n_pcs_graph': 50,\n          'rng_seed': 1\n      }\n      \n      # 1. Preprocessing\n      normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      \n      # 2. Train DANN and get the corrected embedding\n      trained_params, model = train_dann(adata, **dann_params)\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = get_dann_embedding(adata, trained_params, model)\n      \n      # 3. Use the DANN embedding\
    \ as input to the powerful graph construction utility\n      Cg, Dg = build_corrected_graph(adata, Xd=adata.obsm['X_emb'], **graph_params)\n      \n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n      # Also build a simple kNN for standard metrics that might need it\n      import scanpy as sc\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric='cosine')\n      \n      return adata\n```"
