    \ the DANN-generated embedding with my predecessor's sophisticated graph construction logic.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Daedalus V - Run 8: DANN v1 (Proof of Concept)\"\ntags: [\"dann\", \"adversarial\", \"autoencoder\", \"non-linear\", \"daedalus v\"]\nabstract: |\n  This is the first proof-of-concept for a Domain-Adversarial Neural Network (DANN) architecture.\n  The model consists of an encoder, a reconstructor, and an adversarial domain classifier.\n  A Gradient Reversal Layer forces the encoder to learn a batch-invariant latent embedding.\n  This non-linear embedding is then used as input for the proven, SOTA-level graph construction\n  utility. This experiment tests the fundamental viability of the adversarial approach.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from synergy_dann_v1 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as dann_v1_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    # First run of the DANN\
