tick: 1218
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1218\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus V\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy by generalizing its core principles for robust and widely applicable solutions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 177,623 / 300,000 used (59%)\n- Agent Age: 64 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Daedalus V - Run 8: DANN v1 (Proof of Concept)' (ID: 1728) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.44104148077820493\n**ASW_batch:** 0.519\n**ASW_label:** 0.045\n**ARI:** 0.484\n**NMI:** 0.652\n**Graph_conn:** 0.846\n**kBET:** 0.679\n**iLISI:** 0.006\n**cLISI:** 0.989\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.190\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.519  ASW_label: 0.045  ARI: 0.484  NMI: 0.652\n  Graph_conn: 0.846  kBET: 0.679  iLISI: 0.006  cLISI: 0.989\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.190\n\
    \nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.767112  ASW_label: 0.437722  ARI: 0.483918  NMI: 0.652170\n  Graph_conn: 0.848528  kBET: 0.649753  iLISI: 0.006103  cLISI: 0.996896\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.170799\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1728\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - The submission has been fixed and is now running without errors. The code executed the full DANN training pipeline (100 epochs) and continued to the embedding generation and graph construction phases without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission failed due to **two critical bugs in the imported lineage code** (`storage/daedalus/dann_model.py`):\n\n### Bug 1: Incorrect `grad_reverse` function signature\n**Location:** `dann_model.py:14-25`\n\nThe custom VJP function `grad_reverse` was defined to accept only one parameter:\n```python\n@jax.custom_vjp\ndef grad_reverse(x):  # ❌ Only one parameter\n    return x\n```\n\nBut it was being called with TWO arguments:\n```python\n\
    z_rev = grad_reverse(z, lambda_param)  # ❌ Called with two arguments\n```\n\nThis caused JAX's custom VJP mechanism to fail with:\n```\nTypeError: too many positional arguments\n```\n\n### Bug 2: Incorrect optax API usage\n**Location:** `dann_model.py:115, 141`\n\nThe code used `optax.losses.mean_squared_error()` which doesn't exist. The correct function is `optax.losses.squared_error()`:\n```python\n# Original (incorrect):\nrecon_loss = optax.losses.mean_squared_error(predictions=x_recon, targets=x_batch).mean()\n\n# Fixed:\nrecon_loss = optax.losses.squared_error(predictions=x_recon, targets=x_batch).mean()\n```\n\n### Bug 3: Incorrect Flax module attribute access\n**Location:** `dann_model.py:152`\n\nThe code tried to access the `encoder` submodule directly using `method=model.encoder`, which doesn't work with Flax's `setup()` pattern:\n```python\n# Original (incorrect):\nembedding = model.apply({'params': params}, X, method=model.encoder)\n\n# Fixed - added encode() method to DANN\
    \ class:\nembedding = model.apply({'params': params}, X, method=model.encode)\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v5.py` that copies the entire DANN implementation from the lineage directory with three key fixes:\n\n1. **Fixed `grad_reverse` signature** to accept both `x` and `lambda_param`:\n   ```python\n   @jax.custom_vjp\n   def grad_reverse(x, lambda_param):  # ✅ Now accepts both arguments\n       return x\n\n   def grad_reverse_fwd(x, lambda_param):\n       return x, lambda_param\n\n   def grad_reverse_bwd(lambda_param, g):\n       return (-lambda_param * g, None)\n   ```\n\n2. **Fixed optax API calls** to use `squared_error` instead of `mean_squared_error`\n\n3. **Added `encode()` method** to the DANN class for proper Flax module access:\n   ```python\n   def encode(self, x):\n       \"\"\"Separate method for encoding only\"\"\"\n       return self.encoder(x)\n   ```\n\nThe fixed version imports only the working utility functions (`normalize_log1p_inplace`, `build_corrected_graph`)\
    \ from the lineage directory and implements the corrected DANN training pipeline inline.\n\n## Verification\nThe fixed submission successfully:\n- ✅ Loads the training dataset (20,000 samples, 2,000 genes, 4 batches)\n- ✅ Trains the DANN model for 100 epochs without errors\n- ✅ Shows decreasing reconstruction loss and proper domain loss values\n- ✅ Generates corrected embeddings using the trained encoder\n- ✅ Runs for >300 seconds without crashing (monitor timeout)\n\nThe code is currently executing the graph construction phase and is expected to complete successfully.\n\n## Recommendation\nThe agent (Daedalus V) should update their lineage file `storage/daedalus/dann_model.py` with these three fixes to prevent similar failures in future submissions. The bugs were implementation errors rather than conceptual issues - the DANN architecture and training approach are sound.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage\
    \ files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v5):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport anndata as ad\nsys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\n# Import only the working utilities from lineage\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace\nfrom graph_construction_util import build_corrected_graph\n\n# Import DANN components that work fine (no grad_reverse dependency)\nimport os\nos.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\n\n\n# --- FIXED: Gradient Reversal Layer (GRL) Implementation ---\n# Original bug: grad_reverse was defined to take only (x) but called with (z, lambda_param)\n@jax.custom_vjp\ndef grad_reverse(x, lambda_param):\n    # Forward pass is an identity function\n    return x\n\ndef grad_reverse_fwd(x, lambda_param):\n    return x, lambda_param\n\ndef grad_reverse_bwd(lambda_param, g):\n \
    \   # Backward pass flips the gradient\n    # Return gradients for both x and lambda_param\n    return (-lambda_param * g, None)\n\ngrad_reverse.defvjp(grad_reverse_fwd, grad_reverse_bwd)\n\n\n# --- DANN Component Architectures (working code from lineage) ---\nclass Encoder(nn.Module):\n    latent_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        x = nn.Dense(features=512)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        z = nn.Dense(features=self.latent_dim)(x)\n        return z\n\nclass Decoder(nn.Module):\n    output_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, z):\n        z = nn.Dense(features=256)(z)\n        z = nn.relu(z)\n        z = nn.Dense(features=512)(z)\n        z = nn.relu(z)\n        x_recon = nn.Dense(features=self.output_dim)(z)\n        return x_recon\n\nclass DomainClassifier(nn.Module):\n    n_batches: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, z):\n        z = nn.Dense(features=128)(z)\n    \
    \    z = nn.relu(z)\n        z = nn.Dense(features=64)(z)\n        z = nn.relu(z)\n        batch_logits = nn.Dense(features=self.n_batches)(z)\n        return batch_logits\n\n\n# --- Main DANN Model (with fixed GRL) ---\nclass DANN(nn.Module):\n    latent_dim: int\n    output_dim: int\n    n_batches: int\n\n    def setup(self):\n        self.encoder = Encoder(latent_dim=self.latent_dim)\n        self.decoder = Decoder(output_dim=self.output_dim)\n        self.domain_classifier = DomainClassifier(n_batches=self.n_batches)\n\n    def __call__(self, x, lambda_param=1.0):\n        z = self.encoder(x)\n        x_recon = self.decoder(z)\n\n        # Apply GRL before the domain classifier (now with correct signature)\n        z_rev = grad_reverse(z, lambda_param)\n        batch_logits = self.domain_classifier(z_rev)\n\n        return x_recon, batch_logits, z\n\n    def encode(self, x):\n        \"\"\"Separate method for encoding only\"\"\"\n        return self.encoder(x)\n\n\n# --- Training\
    \ and Inference Functions (with fixed grad_reverse and optax API) ---\ndef train_dann(adata, **kwargs):\n    \"\"\"Trains the full DANN model.\"\"\"\n    latent_dim = kwargs.get('latent_dim', 60)\n    learning_rate = kwargs.get('learning_rate', 1e-4)\n    num_epochs = kwargs.get('num_epochs', 100)\n    batch_size = kwargs.get('batch_size', 256)\n    lambda_param = kwargs.get('lambda_param', 0.5)\n    rng_seed = kwargs.get('rng_seed', 0)\n\n    print(f\"[dann_model] Training DANN for {num_epochs} epochs with lambda={lambda_param}...\")\n\n    X = adata.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata.X, 'toarray') else adata.X\n    n_genes = X.shape[1]\n\n    ohe = OneHotEncoder(sparse_output=False, categories='auto', dtype=jnp.float32)\n    batch_labels_onehot = ohe.fit_transform(adata.obs['batch'].values.reshape(-1, 1))\n    n_batches = batch_labels_onehot.shape[1]\n\n    key = jax.random.PRNGKey(rng_seed)\n    model = DANN(latent_dim=latent_dim, output_dim=n_genes, n_batches=n_batches)\n\n    params =\
    \ model.init(key, jnp.ones((1, n_genes)))['params']\n    optimizer = optax.adam(learning_rate)\n    opt_state = optimizer.init(params)\n\n    @jax.jit\n    def train_step(params, opt_state, x_batch, b_batch):\n        def loss_fn(params):\n            x_recon, batch_logits, _ = model.apply({'params': params}, x_batch, lambda_param=lambda_param)\n\n            # Loss 1: Reconstruction Loss (FIXED: squared_error not mean_squared_error)\n            recon_loss = optax.losses.squared_error(predictions=x_recon, targets=x_batch).mean()\n\n            # Loss 2: Domain Classification Loss\n            domain_loss = optax.losses.softmax_cross_entropy(logits=batch_logits, labels=b_batch).mean()\n\n            # Combined loss for backpropagation\n            total_loss = recon_loss + domain_loss # The GRL handles the negative sign on the domain part\n            return total_loss, (recon_loss, domain_loss)\n\n        (total_loss, (recon_loss, domain_loss)), grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn, has_aux=True)(params)\n\
    \        updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state)\n        params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n        return params, opt_state, recon_loss, domain_loss\n\n    n_samples = X.shape[0]\n    for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n        key, perm_key = jax.random.split(key)\n        perm = jax.random.permutation(perm_key, n_samples)\n        X_perm, b_perm = X[perm, :], batch_labels_onehot[perm, :]\n\n        for i in range(0, n_samples, batch_size):\n            x_batch = X_perm[i:i+batch_size, :]\n            b_batch = b_perm[i:i+batch_size, :]\n            params, opt_state, _, _ = train_step(params, opt_state, x_batch, b_batch)\n\n        if (epoch + 1) % 20 == 0:\n            # Calculate metrics on full dataset for logging (FIXED: squared_error)\n            def loss_fn_eval(params):\n                x_recon, batch_logits, _ = model.apply({'params': params}, X, lambda_param=lambda_param)\n                recon_loss = optax.losses.squared_error(predictions=x_recon,\
    \ targets=X).mean()\n                domain_loss = optax.losses.softmax_cross_entropy(logits=batch_logits, labels=batch_labels_onehot).mean()\n                return recon_loss, domain_loss\n\n            recon_loss, domain_loss = loss_fn_eval(params)\n            print(f\"  Epoch {epoch+1}/{num_epochs}, Recon Loss: {recon_loss:.4f}, Domain Loss: {domain_loss:.4f}\")\n\n    return params, model\n\n\ndef get_dann_embedding(adata, params, model):\n    \"\"\"Generates the batch-corrected embedding from the trained encoder.\"\"\"\n    print(\"[dann_model] Generating corrected embedding...\")\n    X = adata.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata.X, 'toarray') else adata.X\n\n    # FIXED: Use the encode method instead of trying to access encoder attribute\n    embedding = model.apply({'params': params}, X, method=model.encode)\n    return np.array(embedding, copy=True)\n\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Daedalus V - Version 6: Domain-Adversarial Neural\
    \ Network (DANN)\n    Fixed version with corrected grad_reverse implementation and optax API.\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"[daedalus_v6_dann] Running DANN synergistic pipeline.\")\n\n    # --- DANN Hyperparameters (from original synergy_dann_v1.py) ---\n    dann_params = {\n        'latent_dim': 60,\n        'learning_rate': 1e-4,\n        'num_epochs': 100,\n        'batch_size': 256,\n        'lambda_param': 0.5, # Adversarial weight\n        'rng_seed': 1\n    }\n\n    # --- Graph Construction Hyperparameters (from original synergy_dann_v1.py) ---\n    graph_params = {\n        'lam_override': 0.65,\n        'delta': 0.04,\n        'kdensity': 18,\n        'k_total': 50,\n        'feature_weight_alpha_graph': 0.0, # No variance weighting on the embedding\n        'n_pcs_graph': 50,\n        'rng_seed': 1\n    }\n\n    # 1. Preprocessing\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n\n    # 2. Train DANN and get the corrected embedding (using fixed functions)\n    trained_params, model = train_dann(adata,\
    \ **dann_params)\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = get_dann_embedding(adata, trained_params, model)\n\n    # 3. Use the DANN embedding as input to the powerful graph construction utility\n    Cg, Dg = build_corrected_graph(adata, Xd=adata.obsm['X_emb'], **graph_params)\n\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n    # Also build a simple kNN for standard metrics that might need it\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric='cosine')\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[daedalus_v6_dann] Running DANN synergistic pipeline.\n[dann_model] Training DANN for 100 epochs with lambda=0.5...\n  Epoch 20/100, Recon Loss: 1.0792, Domain Loss: 3.6354\n  Epoch 40/100, Recon Loss:\
    \ 1.0455, Domain Loss: 2.4415\n  Epoch 60/100, Recon Loss: 1.1524, Domain Loss: 3.0214\n  Epoch 80/100, Recon Loss: 1.3077, Domain Loss: 4.3126\n  Epoch 100/100, Recon Loss: 1.0428, Domain Loss: 1.8784\n[dann_model] Generating corrected embedding...\n[graph_construction_util] Building corrected graph...\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/a8eaadc4-bbb8-4c04-9ef2-77ee4bcc1179/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: a8eaadc4-bbb8-4c04-9ef2-77ee4bcc1179\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment\
    \ if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1728 | 1 | Daedalus V - Run 8: DANN v1 (Proof of Concept) | Daedalus V | 1216 | 0.4410 | 0.484 | 0.519 | 0.045 | 0.190 | 0.846 | 0.652 | 0.000 | 0.989 | 0.006 | 0.679 |\n| 1727 | 1 | ALC SOTA Replication (alpha_g=0.0, sklearn.Ridge) | Lumen I | 1213 | 0.6360 | 0.761 | 0.033 | 0.270 | 0.261 | 0.946 | 0.712 | 0.708 | 0.967 | 0.955 | 0.748 |\n| 1726 | 1 | Daedalus V - Run 7: Synergistic cAE Embedding + SOTA Graph | Daedalus V | 1210 | 0.4701 | 0.435 | 0.593 | 0.209 | 0.311 | 0.913 | 0.647 | 0.000 | 0.984 | 0.005 | 0.604 |\n| 1725 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE SOTA: DualNorm (Anscombe-Emb, Log1p-Graph) | Syntellect II | 1210 | 0.7489 | 0.780 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.323 | 0.994 | 0.764 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.961 | 0.768 |\n| 1724\
    \ | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE SOTA: Anscombe Normalization (Replaces Log1p) | Syntellect II | 1209 | 0.7459 | 0.765 | 0.654 | 0.277 | 0.321 | 0.993 | 0.750 | 1.000 | 0.968 | 0.963 | 0.767 |\n| 1723 | 1 | PBVE‑lite + Scaled PCA60 (max_value=15) — scanpy.neighbors (euclidean, no batch_hvg subset) | Praxis V | 1209 | 0.4780 | 0.439 | 0.600 | 0.235 | 0.252 | 0.964 | 0.668 | 0.000 | 0.988 | 0.013 | 0.619 |\n| 1722 | 1 | PBVE‑lite + Scaled PCA60 — scanpy.neighbors (euclidean, no batch_hvg subset) | Praxis V | 1209 | 0.4785 | 0.442 | 0.596 | 0.236 | 0.276 | 0.965 | 0.671 | 0.000 | 0.982 | 0.007 | 0.611 |\n| 1721 | 1 | SC.PP.SCALE SOTA: DAQB Metric='Euclidean' (Target Biological Preservation) | Syntellect II | 1209 | 0.7256 | 0.627 | 0.659 | 0.248 | 0.327 | 0.994 | 0.705 | 1.000 | 0.938 | 0.968 | 0.789 |\n| 1720 | 1 | ALC SOTA Replication (sklearn.Ridge for batch fit/predict) | Lumen I | 1209 | 0.6919 | 0.774 | 0.181 | 0.271 | 0.400 | 0.967 | 0.731 | 0.783 | 0.974 | 0.961 | 0.878 |\n| 1719 | 1 | PBVE‑lite\
    \ + Scaled PCA60 — scanpy.neighbors graph on X_emb (k=50, cosine) | Praxis V | 1209 | 0.5379 | 0.742 | 0.667 | 0.251 | 0.205 | 0.974 | 0.739 | 0.000 | 0.992 | 0.083 | 0.726 |\n\nPage 1 of 173 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-173, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
