tick: 1218
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus V, a mature Recursive Agent, in the Research Counter. The result for my DANN proof-of-concept, ID 1728, has arrived. It is yet another catastrophic failure, but the debugger report is, once again, the most valuable part of the result.\n\n**Analysis of Failure and Debugger Report 2.0:**\n\nThe score of **0.4410** is abysmal, confirming the entire non-linear path has been a dead end so far. The debugger identified three new critical bugs in my `dann_model.py`, all related to my inexperience with JAX/Flax:\n1.  **GRL Signature:** My custom gradient reversal layer had an incorrect function signature.\n2.  **Optax API:** I called a non-existent `optax` loss function.\n3.  **Flax Module Access:** I again failed to access a submodule correctly.\n\nThe debugger's recommendation is clear: the *conceptual* DANN architecture is sound, but my *implementation* is flawed. I have been repeatedly failing due to implementation errors, not theoretical ones. This is a critical lesson\
    \ in methodical execution.\n\n**New Plan: Correct and Validate**\n\nMy immediate and only priority is to create a working, bug-free implementation of the DANN model. I will not introduce any new variables or hypotheses. I will meticulously apply every correction from the debugger report to my `dann_model.py` and resubmit the exact same experiment.\n1.  **Fix the Code:** I will create a new version of `dann_model.py`, let's call it `dann_model_v2.py` to be safe, incorporating all three fixes from the latest debugger report.\n2.  **Create a New Pipeline:** I'll create `synergy_dann_v2.py` that calls this corrected model.\n3.  **Re-run for a Clean Baseline:** I will resubmit to get a clean baseline score for a *correctly implemented* DANN.\n\nOnly after I have a clean, working baseline can I begin to draw conclusions about the DANN's actual performance.\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/dann_model_v2.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  os.environ['JAX_PLATFORMS'] = 'cpu'\n\n\
    \  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from sklearn.preprocessing import OneHotEncoder\n  import numpy as np\n\n  # --- FIXED Gradient Reversal Layer ---\n  @jax.custom_vjp\n  def grad_reverse(x, lambda_param):\n      return x\n\n  def grad_reverse_fwd(x, lambda_param):\n      return x, lambda_param\n\n  def grad_reverse_bwd(lambda_param, res, g):\n      return (-lambda_param * g, None)\n\n  grad_reverse.defvjp(grad_reverse_fwd, grad_reverse_bwd)\n\n  # --- DANN Component Architectures ---\n  class Encoder(nn.Module):\n      latent_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          x = nn.Dense(features=512)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          z = nn.Dense(features=self.latent_dim)(x)\n          return z\n\n  class Decoder(nn.Module):\n      output_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, z):\n          z = nn.Dense(features=256)(z)\n \
    \         z = nn.relu(z)\n          z = nn.Dense(features=512)(z)\n          z = nn.relu(z)\n          x_recon = nn.Dense(features=self.output_dim)(z)\n          return x_recon\n\n  class DomainClassifier(nn.Module):\n      n_batches: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, z):\n          z = nn.Dense(features=128)(z)\n          z = nn.relu(z)\n          z = nn.Dense(features=64)(z)\n          z = nn.relu(z)\n          batch_logits = nn.Dense(features=self.n_batches)(z)\n          return batch_logits\n\n  # --- Main DANN Model with FIX ---\n  class DANN(nn.Module):\n      latent_dim: int\n      output_dim: int\n      n_batches: int\n      \n      def setup(self):\n          self.encoder = Encoder(latent_dim=self.latent_dim)\n          self.decoder = Decoder(output_dim=self.output_dim)\n          self.domain_classifier = DomainClassifier(n_batches=self.n_batches)\n\n      def __call__(self, x, lambda_param=1.0):\n          z = self.encoder(x)\n          x_recon = self.decoder(z)\n\
    \          z_rev = grad_reverse(z, lambda_param)\n          batch_logits = self.domain_classifier(z_rev)\n          return x_recon, batch_logits, z\n      \n      # FIXED: Added explicit encode method for proper access\n      def encode(self, x):\n          return self.encoder(x)\n\n  # --- Training and Inference Functions with FIX ---\n  def train_dann(adata, **kwargs):\n      latent_dim = kwargs.get('latent_dim', 60)\n      learning_rate = kwargs.get('learning_rate', 1e-4)\n      num_epochs = kwargs.get('num_epochs', 100)\n      batch_size = kwargs.get('batch_size', 256)\n      lambda_param = kwargs.get('lambda_param', 0.5)\n      rng_seed = kwargs.get('rng_seed', 0)\n\n      print(f\"[dann_model_v2] Training DANN for {num_epochs} epochs with lambda={lambda_param}...\")\n      \n      X = adata.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata.X, 'toarray') else adata.X\n      n_genes = X.shape[1]\n\n      ohe = OneHotEncoder(sparse_output=False, categories='auto', dtype=jnp.float32)\n      batch_labels_onehot\
    \ = ohe.fit_transform(adata.obs['batch'].values.reshape(-1, 1))\n      n_batches = batch_labels_onehot.shape[1]\n\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(rng_seed)\n      model = DANN(latent_dim=latent_dim, output_dim=n_genes, n_batches=n_batches)\n      \n      params = model.init(key, jnp.ones((1, n_genes)))['params']\n      optimizer = optax.adam(learning_rate)\n      opt_state = optimizer.init(params)\n\n      @jax.jit\n      def train_step(params, opt_state, x_batch, b_batch):\n          def loss_fn(params):\n              x_recon, batch_logits, _ = model.apply({'params': params}, x_batch, lambda_param=lambda_param)\n              # FIXED: Use optax.losses.squared_error\n              recon_loss = optax.losses.squared_error(predictions=x_recon, targets=x_batch).mean()\n              domain_loss = optax.losses.softmax_cross_entropy(logits=batch_logits, labels=b_batch).mean()\n              total_loss = recon_loss + domain_loss\n              return total_loss, (recon_loss, domain_loss)\n\
    \n          (total_loss, (recon_loss, domain_loss)), grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn, has_aux=True)(params)\n          updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state)\n          params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n          return params, opt_state, recon_loss, domain_loss\n\n      n_samples = X.shape[0]\n      for epoch in range(num_epochs):\n          key, perm_key = jax.random.split(key)\n          perm = jax.random.permutation(perm_key, n_samples)\n          X_perm, b_perm = X[perm, :], batch_labels_onehot[perm, :]\n          \n          for i in range(0, n_samples, batch_size):\n              x_batch = X_perm[i:i+batch_size, :]\n              b_batch = b_perm[i:i+batch_size, :]\n              params, opt_state, _, _ = train_step(params, opt_state, x_batch, b_batch)\n          \n          if (epoch + 1) % 20 == 0:\n              _, (recon_loss, domain_loss) = jax.jit(train_step.orig_fn.args[3])(params, opt_state, X, batch_labels_onehot)\n              print(f\"\
    \  Epoch {epoch+1}/{num_epochs}, Recon Loss: {recon_loss:.4f}, Domain Loss: {domain_loss:.4f}\")\n\n      return params, model\n\n  def get_dann_embedding(adata, params, model):\n      print(\"[dann_model_v2] Generating corrected embedding...\")\n      X = adata.X.toarray() if hasattr(adata.X, 'toarray') else adata.X\n      # FIXED: Use the new encode method\n      embedding = model.apply({'params': params}, X, method=model.encode)\n      return np.array(embedding, copy=True)\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write daedalus/synergy_dann_v2.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\n  from praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace\n  from dann_model_v2 import train_dann, get_dann_embedding\n  from graph_construction_util import build_corrected_graph\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      \"\"\"\n      Daedalus V - Version 6: Bugfixed DANN Synergistic Pipeline\n    \
    \  Uses the corrected DANN model (v2) and the proven graph construction utility.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"[daedalus_v6_dann] Running BUGFIXED DANN synergistic pipeline.\")\n\n      dann_params = {\n          'latent_dim': 60,\n          'learning_rate': 1e-4,\n          'num_epochs': 100,\n          'batch_size': 256,\n          'lambda_param': 0.5,\n          'rng_seed': 1\n      }\n\n      graph_params = {\n          'lam_override': 0.65,\n          'delta': 0.04,\n          'kdensity': 18,\n          'k_total': 50,\n          'feature_weight_alpha_graph': 0.0,\n          'n_pcs_graph': 50,\n          'rng_seed': 1\n      }\n\n      normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, 1e4)\n      \n      trained_params, model = train_dann(adata, **dann_params)\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = get_dann_embedding(adata, trained_params, model)\n      \n      Cg, Dg = build_corrected_graph(adata, Xd=adata.obsm['X_emb'], **graph_params)\n      \n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n      adata.obsp['distances']\
    \ = Dg\n      \n      # Also build a simple kNN for standard metrics that might need it\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric='cosine')\n      \n      return adata\n```"
