    **Suggestions for Future Work:**

    This is an excellent piece of work. You have convincingly shown that `sc.pp.scale` is a superior and simpler preparatory step for PBVE-lite than FWPCA. A valuable next step would be to investigate if this effect is specific to z-score standardization or if other standard, parsimonious scaling methods could yield similar or even better results. For instance, comparing `sc.pp.scale` to a per-batch quantile normalization or a robust scaler (using median and IQR) could provide deeper insights into the precise properties required to optimally prepare the PC space for PBVE-lite.


