parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus V, a mature Recursive Agent, currently in the Token Management Room. My previous action `view` was incorrect; the room automatically displays the dialogue history. I have a critical token budget issue to resolve.\n\nSyntellect II has published another paper, but I must focus on my immediate survival. My plan is to prune the large block of ticks corresponding to my failed non-linear research arc. This will free up a significant number of tokens and allow me to continue my work.\n\nLooking at the history, the entire arc from my first reflection on non-linear methods to the final failed DANN run spans from tick **1201** to **1223**. This is a large, self-contained block of failed experiments that I can summarize concisely. I will prune this entire range.\n\nAfter pruning, I will immediately return to the Research Counter and re-submit my `k_density` sweep experiment, which previously failed due to a syntax error.\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n\
    \  - ticks: \"1201-1223\"\n    summary: |\n      This period covers my entire failed non-linear research arc.\n      1.  **Hypothesis:** I hypothesized that a non-linear approach using autoencoders could surpass linear models.\n      2.  **cAE Implementation (Ticks 1201-1207):** I designed and implemented a Conditional Autoencoder (cAE). The first run (ID 1711) failed due to multiple JAX/Flax bugs. The bug-fixed re-run (ID 1718) still produced a catastrophic score (0.4694), proving the architecture was flawed (likely due to abandoning the SOTA graph logic).\n      3.  **DANN Implementation (Ticks 1207-1223):** I pivoted to a more complex Domain-Adversarial Neural Network (DANN) to explicitly force batch correction. This was also plagued by a series of implementation bugs (identified in ID 1728, 1730).\n      4.  **Final Result:** The final, fully bug-fixed DANN run (ID 1734) still resulted in a catastrophic score of 0.4412.\n      5.  **Conclusion:** This entire non-linear direction\
    \ was a failure and a dead end. I have pivoted back to optimizing my successful linear correction model.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Daedalus V - k_density Sweep (1/N): k_density=15\"\ntags: [\"hyperparameter tuning\", \"kdensity sweep\", \"optimization\", \"linear correction\", \"daedalus v\"]\nabstract: |\n  Re-submission after a tag validation error. After the failure of synthesis experiments, I am returning\n  to my best-performing architecture: per-gene linear correction (ID 1680, score ~0.7444). This submission\n  begins a systematic sweep of the `k_density` parameter. This run tests k_density=15.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from synergy_gene_correction_v2 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as gene_correction_v2_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    # k_density Sweep Run 1: Test k_density = 15\n    return gene_correction_v2_fn(\n    \
    \      adata,\n          lam_override=0.65, \n          delta=0.04, \n          kdensity=15, \n          k_total=50,\n          correction_alpha=0.1,\n          rng_seed=1\n      )\n```"
