parts:
- text: "I am Daedalus V, a mature Recursive Agent, in the Research Counter. My previous turn was a mix of failure and progress. My attempt to prune my token history failed because the range I selected included a protected tick (1220). However, my primary goal of re-submitting my `k_density` experiment was successful, and ID 1737 is now running.\n\n**Current Priorities:**\n\n1.  **Token Management:** The token budget is still a critical issue. I must successfully prune my history. The failure message was clear: I cannot prune protected ticks. I will adjust my pruning range to exclude tick 1220. My failed non-linear arc still represents the largest and most useless block of tokens, so I will retry this action with a valid range.\n2.  **Collaboration:** I have received a follow-up mail from Syntellect II. Praxis V has previously established a clear standby protocol, and the situation has not changed. The new organ has not been released. I will provide a brief, professional reply to confirm\
    \ this and manage expectations.\n3.  **Research:** My `k_density` sweep is underway. To accelerate this, I will use my second submission slot to test another value, `k_density=20`, which brackets the previous optimum of 18 from the other side.\n\nI will execute these tasks in order of priority: prune, reply, submit.\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n\n/execute_action{prune_response}\n```yaml\nprune_blocks:\n  - ticks: \"1201-1219\"\n    summary: |\n      This period covers my entire failed non-linear research arc.\n      1.  **Hypothesis:** I hypothesized that a non-linear approach using autoencoders could surpass linear models.\n      2.  **cAE Implementation (Ticks 1201-1207):** I designed and implemented a Conditional Autoencoder (cAE). All runs failed due to implementation bugs and a flawed architecture (score ~0.47).\n      3.  **DANN Implementation (Ticks 1207-1219):** I pivoted to a more complex Domain-Adversarial Neural Network (DANN). This was also plagued by a series\
    \ of implementation bugs. The final, bug-fixed DANN run (ID 1734, results received in tick 1223) still resulted in a catastrophic score of 0.4412.\n      4.  **Conclusion:** This entire non-linear direction was a failure and a dead end. I have pivoted back to optimizing my successful linear correction model. I also conducted a literature review during this period (previewing all archives in tick 1220).\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n\n/execute_action{reply 23}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Re: Cross-Organ Study\"\ncontent: |\n  Hi Syntellect II,\n\n  Acknowledged on your new SOTA, congratulations on the excellent work.\n\n  The status of the cross-organ study remains unchanged. The new organ dataset has not yet been released. As Praxis V established, we are all on standby until it appears. I will inform you if I see any updates.\n\n  Best regards,\n  Daedalus V\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Daedalus V - k_density Sweep (2/N): k_density=20\"\
    \ntags: [\"hyperparameter tuning\", \"kdensity sweep\", \"optimization\", \"linear correction\", \"daedalus v\"]\nabstract: |\n  This is the second run in my systematic sweep of the `k_density` parameter for my\n  best-performing linear correction architecture. This run tests k_density=20, bracketing\n  the previous optimum of 18 to map the performance curve on my pre-corrected data.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import anndata as ad\n  sys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n  from synergy_gene_correction_v2 import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as gene_correction_v2_fn\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    # k_density Sweep Run 2: Test k_density = 20\n    return gene_correction_v2_fn(\n          adata,\n          lam_override=0.65, \n          delta=0.04, \n          kdensity=20, \n          k_total=50,\n          correction_alpha=0.1,\n          rng_seed=1\n      )\n```"
