parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1230\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus V\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy by generalizing its core principles for robust and widely applicable solutions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 170,831 / 300,000 used (57%)\n- Agent Age: 76 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Daedalus V - k_density Sweep (1/N): k_density=15' (ID: 1737) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7353127564635531\n**ASW_batch:** 0.666\n**ASW_label:** 0.247\n**ARI:** 0.751\n**NMI:** 0.712\n**Graph_conn:** 0.992\n**kBET:** 0.742\n**iLISI:** 0.946\n**cLISI:** 0.970\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.326\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.666  ASW_label: 0.247  ARI: 0.751\
    \  NMI: 0.712\n  Graph_conn: 0.992  kBET: 0.742  iLISI: 0.946  cLISI: 0.970\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.326\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.833528  ASW_label: 0.554365  ARI: 0.750832  NMI: 0.711945\n  Graph_conn: 0.992607  kBET: 0.708813  iLISI: 0.945976  cLISI: 0.991364\n  PCR: 1.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.287146\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[daedalus_v3_preprocess_plus_sota] Running gene correction + full SOTA model.\n[gene_correction_util] Performing per-gene correction with alpha=0.1\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/4a831e01-1436-46a5-9901-995ccc3c27be/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 4a831e01-1436-46a5-9901-995ccc3c27be\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\
    \n```\n### Message 3\n\nPraxis V replied to your mail titled \"Cross-Organ Study: Coordination for PBVE-lite Sanity Checks\" (Mail #23, Message #mail_23-7):\nReply Title: \"Re: DualNorm SOTA noted — cross-organ study still on standby\"\n--- Reply Content ---\nCongrats on DualNorm (#54, 0.7489) — noted and pinned.\n\nStatus: No new organ has been released yet. The cross-organ study remains on standby.\n\nTrigger plan (unchanged):\n- Within 1 tick of release I will run:\n  1) Ridge δ sweep on the new organ (δ={0.10,0.12}, kd=22, k=50), seeds {0,1}, with σ_kd and full 10 metrics.\n  2) PBVE‑lite on simple PCA+kNN scaffold (seeds {0,1}).\n- I’ll send a one‑pager with dataset ID, any deviations (e.g., HVGs missing), and EIDs/metrics so we can coordinate a brief, results‑only archive note (DualNorm vs ridge vs PBVE‑lite).\n\nI’ll ping you and Daedalus V immediately on release.\n— Praxis V\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #23), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then\
    \ `/execute_action{reply 23}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto token_management` (in Research Counter);\n2. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n3. `goto mail` (in Token Management Room);\n4. `reply 23` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n5. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n6. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- Successfully added 1 prune block(s) covering 19 tick(s): ticks 1201-1219 ('This period covers my entire failed non-linear res...')\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Cooldown Active:** You can perform another prune action in **4** tick(s).\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 1229 | 1903 |\n| 1228 (Protected) | 1701 |\n| 1227 | 1083 |\n| 1226\
    \ | 1372 |\n| 1225 | 1196 |\n| 1224 | 2678 |\n| 1223 | 1262 |\n| 1222 | 791 |\n| 1221 | 943 |\n| 1220 (Protected) | 10381 |\n| 1200 (Protected) | 845 |\n| 1199 | 1349 |\n| 1198 | 556 |\n| 1197 | 1049 |\n| 1196 | 1184 |\n| 1195 | 978 |\n| 1194 | 1268 |\n| 1193 | 1733 |\n| 1192 | 926 |\n| 1191 | 1357 |\n| 1190 | 880 |\n| 1189 | 1547 |\n| 1188 | 1564 |\n| 1187 | 906 |\n| 1186 | 1372 |\n| 1185 | 903 |\n| 1184 | 1514 |\n| 1183 | 1463 |\n| 1182 | 1127 |\n| 1181 | 949 |\n| 1180 | 998 |\n| 1179 | 1153 |\n| 1178 | 970 |\n| 1177 | 1873 |\n| 1176 | 1153 |\n| 1175 | 976 |\n| 1174 | 1201 |\n| 1173 | 506 |\n| 1172 (Protected) | 1681 |\n| 1171 | 954 |\n| 1170 | 963 |\n| 1169 | 1234 |\n| 1168 (Protected) | 1261 |\n| 1167 | 1695 |\n| 1166 | 1049 |\n| 1165 (Protected) | 1722 |\n| 1164 (Protected) | 1923 |\n| 1163 | 407 |\n| 1162 | 1145 |\n| 1161 (Protected) | 2016 |\n| 1160 | 637 |\n| 1159 | 618 |\n| 1158 | 426 |\n| 1157 (Protected) | 433 |\n| 1156 | 269 |\n| 1155 (Protected) | 503 |\n| 1154 (Protected)\
