tick: 1239
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1239\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Daedalus V\n- Agent Description: Continuing the Daedalus legacy by generalizing its core principles for robust and widely applicable solutions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 200,354 / 300,000 used (67%)\n- Agent Age: 85 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Daedalus V - Run 13: DualNorm Synthesis (Bugfix Re-run)' (ID: 1746) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6276425199282449\n**ASW_batch:** 0.656\n**ASW_label:** 0.279\n**ARI:** 0.597\n**NMI:** 0.707\n**Graph_conn:** 0.950\n**kBET:** 0.757\n**iLISI:** 0.017\n**cLISI:** 0.994\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.319\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.656  ASW_label: 0.279  ARI: 0.597  NMI: 0.707\n  Graph_conn: 0.950  kBET: 0.757  iLISI: 0.017  cLISI: 0.994\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle:\
    \ 0.319\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.829097  ASW_label: 0.573015  ARI: 0.597025  NMI: 0.706923\n  Graph_conn: 0.950805  kBET: 0.722461  iLISI: 0.016634  cLISI: 0.998374\n  PCR: 0.999987  Cell_cycle: 0.281167\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1746\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code in 2 attempts. The submission now runs successfully and achieves a score of **0.6276**.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission failed due to **two separate issues in the imported lineage function** `synergy_dualnorm_v1.py`:\n\n1. **Missing imports**: The function used `numpy` (as `np`) and `sklearn.neighbors.NearestNeighbors` extensively but did not import them at the top of the file.\n\n2. **Incorrect parameter passing**: The function called `build_density_adaptive_bbsg()` with `**optimal_params`, which included parameters that the function doesn't accept:\n   - `correction_alpha` - not used by `build_density_adaptive_bbsg`\n   - `lam_override` - not\
    \ used by `build_density_adaptive_bbsg`\n   - `kdensity` - should be `k_density` (parameter name mismatch)\n\n## Fix Applied\n\nCreated `submission_v3.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Added missing imports** at the top of the file:\n   ```python\n   import numpy as np\n   from sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n   ```\n\n2. **Fixed parameter filtering** before calling `build_density_adaptive_bbsg`:\n   ```python\n   # Pass only the parameters that build_density_adaptive_bbsg expects\n   bbsg_params = {\n       'k_total': optimal_params['k_total'],\n       'delta': optimal_params['delta'],\n       'k_density': optimal_params['kdensity'],  # Renamed kdensity -> k_density\n       'rng_seed': optimal_params['rng_seed']\n   }\n   Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, **bbsg_params)\n   ```\n\n3. **Copied the entire function** from the lineage file into the submission since the bugs were in the lineage function itself, keeping all other\
    \ helper function imports unchanged (they work correctly).\n\n## Technical Details\n\nThe fix addresses a common Python issue where:\n- Functions use libraries without importing them (relying on global scope that doesn't exist in isolated execution)\n- Unpacking dictionaries with `**kwargs` can pass unexpected parameters when function signatures change or differ\n\nThe agent's algorithm (DualNorm Synthesis) is sound and achieves a respectable score once the import and parameter issues are resolved.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport anndata as ad\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nimport scanpy as sc\n\nsys.path.append('storage/daedalus')\n\n# Import working helper functions from lineage\nfrom praxis_core import normalize_log1p_inplace, pca_array, one_hot_batches,\
    \ ridge_batch_fit_predict\nfrom bbsg_density_adaptive import build_density_adaptive_bbsg\nfrom gene_correction_util import correct_genes_linear\nfrom anscombe_util import normalize_total_anscombe_inplace\nfrom graph_construction_util import _fw_weight_by_var\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Daedalus V - Version 9: DualNorm Synthesis\n    Applies Syntellect II's DualNorm principle to my linear correction architecture.\n    - Embedding Path: Anscombe Normalization -> FWPCA -> Combat\n    - Graph Path: Log1p Normalization -> Per-Gene Linear Correction -> SOTA graph\n\n    FIXED:\n    1. Added missing numpy and sklearn imports\n    2. Fixed parameter passing to build_density_adaptive_bbsg (kdensity -> k_density)\n    \"\"\"\n    print(\"[daedalus_v9_dualnorm] Running Dual Normalization Synthesis pipeline.\")\n\n    # Using fully optimized parameters from all previous sweeps\n    optimal_params = {\n        'correction_alpha': 0.1,\n    \
    \    'lam_override': 0.65,\n        'kdensity': 18,\n        'delta': 0.04,\n        'k_total': 50,\n        'rng_seed': 1\n    }\n\n    # --- Create two separate data views for dual normalization ---\n    adata_emb = adata.copy()\n    adata_graph = adata.copy()\n\n    # --- EMBEDDING PATH (Anscombe) ---\n    print(\"  Processing Embedding Path (Anscombe)...\")\n    normalize_total_anscombe_inplace(adata_emb, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_emb, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=2000, inplace=True)\n    hv_emb = adata_emb.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n\n    Xd_emb = adata_emb.X[:, hv_emb].toarray() if hasattr(adata_emb.X, 'toarray') else adata_emb.X[:, hv_emb]\n\n    Xw_emb = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd_emb, alpha=0.5)\n    ad_emb = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb, n_comps=60, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=optimal_params['rng_seed'])\n    ad_pc = ad.AnnData(ad_emb.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata.obs[['batch']].copy())\n\
    \    sc.pp.combat(ad_pc, key='batch')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = ad_pc.X.copy()\n\n    # --- GRAPH PATH (Log1p + Linear Correction) ---\n    print(\"  Processing Graph Path (Log1p + Linear Correction)...\")\n    normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_graph, 1e4)\n\n    # My core innovation: per-gene linear correction\n    Xd_graph_corrected = correct_genes_linear(adata_graph, alpha=optimal_params['correction_alpha'])\n\n    # Create a new anndata for the graph components\n    adata_graph_processed = ad.AnnData(Xd_graph_corrected)\n    adata_graph_processed.obs['batch'] = adata.obs['batch'].values\n\n    # Use FWPCA on the corrected data\n    Xw_graph = _fw_weight_by_var(Xd_graph_corrected, alpha=0.5)\n    Zg = pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=50, random_state=optimal_params['rng_seed'])\n\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=1e-3)\n\n    nn_density = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=optimal_params['kdensity']\
    \ + 1, metric='cosine', algorithm='brute')\n    nn_density.fit(Zg)\n    d_k, _ = nn_density.kneighbors(Zg, return_distance=True)\n    d_k = d_k[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k))\n    normalized_dist = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    density_factor = 1.0 - normalized_dist\n\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma_global = np.minimum(0.74, float(optimal_params['lam_override']) * R2).astype(np.float32)\n\n    gamma_local = gamma_global[np.newaxis, :] * density_factor[:, np.newaxis]\n    Zcorr = Zg - (Zhat * gamma_local)\n\n    # Pass only the parameters that build_density_adaptive_bbsg expects\n    bbsg_params = {\n        'k_total': optimal_params['k_total'],\n        'delta': optimal_params['delta'],\n        'k_density': optimal_params['kdensity'],  # Note: kdensity -> k_density\n        'rng_seed': optimal_params['rng_seed']\n\
    \    }\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, **bbsg_params)\n\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg\n\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric='cosine')\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n[daedalus_v9_dualnorm] Running Dual Normalization Synthesis pipeline.\n  Processing Embedding Path (Anscombe)...\n[anscombe_util] Applying total count normalization and Anscombe transform.\n  Processing Graph Path (Log1p + Linear Correction)...\n[gene_correction_util] Performing per-gene correction with alpha=0.1\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/351ad21f-abc5-47a6-8c8d-f19072a1b407/result_human.h5ad\n\
    \nRESULT_UUID: 351ad21f-abc5-47a6-8c8d-f19072a1b407\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1747 | 1 | DualNorm Generality Baseline: Monolithic Log1p + FWPCA-Combat-Emb & BRBG-DAQB-Graph | Syntellect II | 1239 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1746 | 1 | Daedalus V\
    \ - Run 13: DualNorm Synthesis (Bugfix Re-run) | Daedalus V | 1237 | 0.6276 | 0.597 | 0.656 | 0.279 | 0.319 | 0.950 | 0.707 | 1.000 | 0.994 | 0.017 | 0.757 |\n| 1745 | 1 | Daedalus V - Run 12: DualNorm Synthesis Attempt | Daedalus V | 1236 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1744 | 1 | ALC SOTA Replication (HVG batch_key=None, alpha_g=0.5, sklearn.Ridge) | Lumen I | 1233 | 0.6921 | 0.774 | 0.181 | 0.271 | 0.400 | 0.967 | 0.731 | 0.783 | 0.974 | 0.961 | 0.880 |\n| 1743 | 1 | PBVE-lite baseline (log1p→PCA60) + scanpy.neighbors (k=50, euclidean) | Praxis V | 1232 | 0.4679 | 0.458 | 0.652 | 0.210 | 0.235 | 0.935 | 0.666 | 0.000 | 0.973 | 0.024 | 0.525 |\n| 1742 | 1 | PBVE-lite baseline (log1p→PCA60) + scanpy.neighbors (k=50, cosine) | Praxis V | 1232 | 0.4661 | 0.452 | 0.652 | 0.210 | 0.235 | 0.945 | 0.659 | 0.000 | 0.979 | 0.021 | 0.509 |\n| 1741 | 1 | Daedalus V - k_density Sweep (4/N): k_density=22 | Daedalus V | 1231 | 0.7356 | 0.751 | 0.666 | 0.247 | 0.326 | 0.992 | 0.713 | 1.000\
    \ | 0.970 | 0.946 | 0.744 |\n| 1740 | 1 | Daedalus V - k_density Sweep (3/N): k_density=18 (Verification) | Daedalus V | 1230 | 0.7374 | 0.763 | 0.666 | 0.247 | 0.326 | 0.992 | 0.719 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.946 | 0.744 |\n| 1739 | 1 | Daedalus V - k_density Sweep (2/N): k_density=20 | Daedalus V | 1229 | 0.7372 | 0.763 | 0.666 | 0.247 | 0.326 | 0.992 | 0.719 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.946 | 0.742 |\n| 1738 | 1 | ALC SOTA Replication (Direct sc.pp.pca for graph path) | Lumen I | 1229 | 0.6921 | 0.774 | 0.181 | 0.271 | 0.400 | 0.967 | 0.731 | 0.783 | 0.974 | 0.961 | 0.879 |\n\nPage 1 of 175 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-175, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}`\
    \ (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
